1
00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:18,420
The latest ceasefire came too late to save these villages...

2
00:00:23,270 --> 00:00:26,060
Today President Clinton voiced,

3
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:28,930
concerns at the deteriorating situation in Sarajevo...

4
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:37,940
When people ask me, good listeners, why do I hate all the Tutsi,

5
00:00:38,010 --> 00:00:40,880
I say, "Read our history. "

6
00:00:40,950 --> 00:00:43,880
The Tutsi were collaborators for the Belgian colonists.

7
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:46,950
They stole our Hutu land, they whipped us.

8
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:50,120
Now they have come back, these Tutsi rebels.

9
00:00:50,190 --> 00:00:53,450
They are cockroaches. They are murderers.

10
00:00:53,530 --> 00:00:58,130
Rwanda is our Hutu land. We are the majority.

11
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:01,730
They are a minority of traitors and invaders.

12
00:01:01,810 --> 00:01:07,650
We will squash the infestation. We will wipe out the RPF rebels.

13
00:01:07,710 --> 00:01:11,200
This is RTLM, Hutu Power Radio.

14
00:01:11,290 --> 00:01:14,370
Stay alert. Watch your neighbors.

15
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:30,850
基加利  １９９４

16
00:01:33,810 --> 00:01:37,300
-Mr. Rusesabagina, thank you. -Good to see you, sir.

17
00:01:49,550 --> 00:01:50,540
Thank you.

18
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:53,020
These are for you, sir. They're fresh from Havana.

19
00:01:53,090 --> 00:01:56,080
Wonderful. Next time you are there, tell Fidel that I said hello.

20
00:01:56,970 --> 00:01:58,290
Good to see you gentlemen.

21
00:02:01,850 --> 00:02:06,940
卢 旺 达 饭 店

22
00:02:22,890 --> 00:02:25,440
That is a fine cigar, sir.

23
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:27,850
This is a Cohiba cigar.

24
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:31,870
-Each one is worth 10,000 francs. -10,000 francs?

25
00:02:31,930 --> 00:02:35,220
Yes, yes. But it is worth more to me than 10,000 francs.

26
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:36,920
What do you mean, sir?

27
00:02:39,630 --> 00:02:43,730
If I give a businessman 10,000 francs, what does that matter to him?

28
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:47,750
He is rich. But, if I give him a Cohiba cigar

29
00:02:47,810 --> 00:02:52,510
straight from Havana, Cuba... Hey, that is style, Dube.

30
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:54,380
Style.

31
00:03:04,330 --> 00:03:07,320
Cohiba... a fantastic cigar.

32
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:09,530
The best, eh?

33
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:12,260
So, you're going to join us at the rally today?

34
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:16,170
I will try my best, George,

35
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:19,830
but these days I have no time for rallies and politics.

36
00:03:19,910 --> 00:03:23,310
Politics is power, Paul. Hutu power.

37
00:03:23,390 --> 00:03:24,740
And money.

38
00:03:29,090 --> 00:03:31,250
It's time for you to join your people.

39
00:03:32,790 --> 00:03:34,080
Thank you, George.

40
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:36,950
But time is also money.

41
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:41,130
I need six extra cases of beer today,

42
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:43,030
along with the regular order.

43
00:03:46,170 --> 00:03:48,830
-Business is good at the hotel. -It is very good.

44
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:52,040
I'm always glad to see you, Paul.

45
00:03:58,790 --> 00:04:01,370
Put that back! Put that back! That's not beer!

46
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:09,210
-You, clean this up. -Yes, sir. Come on.

47
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:11,990
Paul, don't worry about the Carlsberg.

48
00:04:12,060 --> 00:04:14,820
I'll give you Heineken, and I won't charge you extra.

49
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:15,890
Thank you.

50
00:04:20,370 --> 00:04:23,970
A bargain buy from China... ten cents each.

51
00:04:25,010 --> 00:04:27,410
You know, I'll get at least fifty.

52
00:04:28,080 --> 00:04:29,380
At least.

53
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:39,350
George Rutaganda is a bad man.

54
00:04:39,420 --> 00:04:42,260
I've heard him on the radio telling the Hutus to kill all the Tutsis.

55
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:46,750
Rutaganda and his people, they are fools, Dube.

56
00:04:46,830 --> 00:04:49,100
Their time is soon over.

57
00:04:49,170 --> 00:04:51,130
Anyway, this is business.

58
00:04:57,100 --> 00:05:00,730
-Oh, no. It's the Interhamwe. -Do as they say. Pull over.

59
00:05:20,930 --> 00:05:23,000
No, no, sit up, Dube. Sit up.

60
00:05:23,070 --> 00:05:25,060
Smile, Dube. Don't attract attention to yourself.

61
00:05:25,130 --> 00:05:29,040
Some of these men are my neighbors. They know that I'm Tutsi.

62
00:05:29,110 --> 00:05:31,630
Just smile as if they are friends, Dube.

63
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:38,950
-I know this man! -Are you a Tutsi?

64
00:05:39,010 --> 00:05:40,350
What are you doing here?

65
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:44,110
No, no. Hutu power. Hutu power, Hutu power!

66
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:47,280
Okay. Yes!

67
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:52,920
Get out of here.

68
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:03,230
There's water coming from the box.

69
00:06:03,310 --> 00:06:05,460
Park here. We'll go in the front.

70
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:11,150
Gregoire, please help with this water.

71
00:06:12,350 --> 00:06:13,650
Gregoire!

72
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:15,350
Deal with this right away.

73
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:18,550
-We were hoping to go see the gorilla. -You must contact our safari desk.

74
00:06:20,160 --> 00:06:22,490
Dube, this is the lobby.

75
00:06:22,570 --> 00:06:25,190
-What's going on? -I am sorry, sir. It is an emergency.

76
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,230
Oh, shit! Oh, sorry, sir.

77
00:06:34,740 --> 00:06:36,830
Ten alive, twelve are dead.

78
00:06:39,370 --> 00:06:40,530
All right.

79
00:06:41,510 --> 00:06:43,350
But save the shells.

80
00:06:43,410 --> 00:06:44,900
Fill them with...

81
00:06:45,850 --> 00:06:49,010
...a stuffing. The good meat and something local.

82
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:52,860
-Cassava? -And... the fish.

83
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:55,120
-And tipali. -Yes.

84
00:06:55,190 --> 00:06:58,960
We'll call it "fresh lobster in a cassava and tipali crust. "

85
00:06:59,030 --> 00:07:00,020
Dube.

86
00:07:00,090 --> 00:07:01,500
Style, sir.

87
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:03,030
Yes, sir.

88
00:07:05,870 --> 00:07:09,970
The problem is, General Bizimungu, I have information

89
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:15,240
that the Interhamwe militia will not heed the peace agreement.

90
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:18,870
Colonel, the U.N. Need not worry about the Interhamwe.

91
00:07:18,940 --> 00:07:20,170
We will control them.

92
00:07:20,250 --> 00:07:22,420
-General. -Paul.

93
00:07:22,490 --> 00:07:24,570
This scotch is exceptional.

94
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:28,420
It is our most popular single malt. I knew you'd like it.

95
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:30,360
Colonel Oliver, it is a pleasure to see you, sir.

96
00:07:30,420 --> 00:07:32,420
Good to see you, Paul.

97
00:07:33,030 --> 00:07:36,020
General, let me recommend the lobster for lunch today.

98
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:38,070
It is spectacular... straight off the plane.

99
00:07:38,130 --> 00:07:41,040
Fresh lobster in Kigali. You do us proud, Paul.

100
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:42,090
Thank you.

101
00:07:42,180 --> 00:07:45,070
I left a little something for you at the coat check.

102
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:47,580
Excuse me, gentlemen.

103
00:07:49,750 --> 00:07:51,980
I need flour. Give me two bags of flour.

104
00:07:53,520 --> 00:07:55,610
Okay, the plates are ready. Here they come.

105
00:07:58,060 --> 00:07:59,710
Good afternoon, ladies.

106
00:07:59,790 --> 00:08:02,350
Elizabeth, please put these in the general's briefcase.

107
00:08:02,430 --> 00:08:03,720
Yes, sir.

108
00:08:05,530 --> 00:08:07,120
This is RTLM, Hutu Power Radio.

109
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:10,500
I have a message for our president.

110
00:08:10,570 --> 00:08:14,470
Beware. Do not trust the Tutsi rebels.

111
00:08:14,540 --> 00:08:17,060
Do not shake the hand that will stab you.

112
00:08:17,140 --> 00:08:18,400
They will treat you...

113
00:08:19,310 --> 00:08:21,200
...reporting from Kigali, Rwanda,

114
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:22,250
where tensions are high

115
00:08:22,310 --> 00:08:25,480
as the deadline for the U.N.-brokered peace agreement approaches.

116
00:08:29,980 --> 00:08:31,290
Hello, Mr. Paul.

117
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:46,490
Hello, Jeremiah.

118
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,170
Hello, sir.

119
00:08:53,580 --> 00:08:55,630
-Good to see you, Paul. -Odette.

120
00:08:57,380 --> 00:08:58,870
See you soon.

121
00:09:00,850 --> 00:09:02,910
So your brother and the girls are here.

122
00:09:02,990 --> 00:09:04,190
Yes.

123
00:09:05,380 --> 00:09:06,420
One, two, three...

124
00:09:06,490 --> 00:09:08,360
Oh, Carine!

125
00:09:09,020 --> 00:09:10,990
Okay, Anais, let me see. Your turn.

126
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:12,500
One, two, three...

127
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:17,460
Who is the winner? Oh, it doesn't matter.

128
00:09:17,530 --> 00:09:19,290
I have chocolates. Who wants chocolates?

129
00:09:19,370 --> 00:09:20,490
Hey, Papa, watch this.

130
00:09:23,780 --> 00:09:26,970
Oh, my goodness. Well, here, chocolates, chocolates. Who wants?

131
00:09:27,540 --> 00:09:29,740
Say thank you to your Uncle Paul.

132
00:09:29,810 --> 00:09:32,910
-Please, not before dinner. -Not before dinner, Mama says.

133
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:35,110
-Thank you. -Okay, okay.

134
00:09:35,180 --> 00:09:36,450
Let's go in.

135
00:09:42,690 --> 00:09:45,850
Things are very slow at the shop. How are things at the hotel?

136
00:09:45,940 --> 00:09:49,090
Very busy. Many people visiting the gorillas.

137
00:09:49,170 --> 00:09:51,960
A lot of foreign press arriving for the peace acc...

138
00:09:52,030 --> 00:09:54,560
-What? -There are soldiers.

139
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:57,200
-Where? -On the street.

140
00:10:01,270 --> 00:10:04,110
I'll go see what's happening. It's all right.

141
00:10:07,020 --> 00:10:11,010
-We know you are Tutsi. -Please, sir, this is my husband.

142
00:10:11,090 --> 00:10:13,480
-He's just a gardener. -He's been spying for the rebels.

143
00:10:13,560 --> 00:10:16,320
-No, we do not know any rebels. -You will come with us!

144
00:10:16,390 --> 00:10:19,420
No, we are telling the truth. We do not know any...

145
00:10:20,290 --> 00:10:21,730
-What is it? -Shut up!

146
00:10:21,790 --> 00:10:24,460
Tatiana, go back in the house. You must go back.

147
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:26,510
-You mustn't be out here. -It's Victor.

148
00:10:29,370 --> 00:10:31,430
No, Captain, you see...

149
00:10:31,510 --> 00:10:34,640
It's not me. It's not me. Captain, Captain.

150
00:10:34,710 --> 00:10:37,270
Why are you taking him away? Please, please.

151
00:10:37,350 --> 00:10:39,780
-I know, I know, but it's not me. -You Tutsi fuckers.

152
00:10:40,950 --> 00:10:42,420
No! No!

153
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:43,820
We must do something.

154
00:10:43,890 --> 00:10:45,580
-Do what? -Call someone.

155
00:10:45,650 --> 00:10:48,560
I'm not going. I'm not going.

156
00:10:48,620 --> 00:10:49,640
No!

157
00:10:55,660 --> 00:10:57,860
Get him in the truck. Now!

158
00:10:58,970 --> 00:11:00,670
We must do something.

159
00:11:00,740 --> 00:11:02,790
Please help him!

160
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:05,310
Oh, Victor!

161
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:06,860
Victor!

162
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:08,810
There is nothing we can do.

163
00:11:09,840 --> 00:11:12,680
-You must stay the night, Thomas. -Yes.

164
00:11:15,650 --> 00:11:17,480
No!

165
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:21,380
Why would they arrest Victor?

166
00:11:23,630 --> 00:11:25,490
He has no politics.

167
00:11:26,330 --> 00:11:29,090
-He's a gardener. -Who knows, Tatsi?

168
00:11:30,270 --> 00:11:31,430
Who knows?

169
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:35,400
Someone who didn't like him denounced him as a rebel spy.

170
00:11:36,740 --> 00:11:38,460
Happens all the time now.

171
00:11:40,410 --> 00:11:45,440
Maybe you could call one of your contacts in the army.

172
00:11:46,180 --> 00:11:47,700
It wouldn't help.

173
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:51,110
You could ask as a favor.

174
00:11:51,190 --> 00:11:53,350
No, I could not.

175
00:11:54,690 --> 00:11:59,500
Tatsi, all day long I work to please this officer,

176
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:03,430
that diplomat, some tourist, to store up favors

177
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:06,130
so if there is a time when we need help,

178
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:08,260
I have powerful people I can call upon.

179
00:12:08,340 --> 00:12:10,670
But Victor was a good neighbor.

180
00:12:10,740 --> 00:12:15,040
He is not family. Family is all that matters.

181
00:12:15,740 --> 00:12:20,910
Please, please, leave these things to my good judgment.

182
00:12:36,700 --> 00:12:39,040
This assignment is bullshit.

183
00:12:39,100 --> 00:12:42,160
Come on. A few days in a nice hotel, no one shooting at us?

184
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:47,850
Gentlemen, welcome to the Mille Collines.

185
00:12:47,910 --> 00:12:50,140
I am Paul Rusesabagina, the house manager.

186
00:12:50,210 --> 00:12:52,050
-How you doing? -Nice to meet you.

187
00:12:52,110 --> 00:12:54,310
Anything that you need, please find me.

188
00:12:54,380 --> 00:12:55,750
-Thank you. -Certainly.

189
00:13:03,330 --> 00:13:07,390
So, what is the actual difference between a Hutu and a Tutsi?

190
00:13:07,460 --> 00:13:11,870
According to the Belgian colonists, the Tutsis are taller and more elegant.

191
00:13:11,930 --> 00:13:14,900
It was the Belgians that created the division.

192
00:13:14,970 --> 00:13:16,460
How?

193
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:19,870
They picked people, those with thinner noses, lighter skin.

194
00:13:19,940 --> 00:13:22,010
They used to measure the width of people's noses.

195
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:24,600
The Belgians used the Tutsis to run the country.

196
00:13:24,690 --> 00:13:27,010
Then when they left, they left the power to the Hutus,

197
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:29,350
and of course the Hutus took revenge

198
00:13:29,420 --> 00:13:31,680
on the elite Tutsis for years of repression.

199
00:13:31,750 --> 00:13:33,550
Am I telling the truth, Paul?

200
00:13:33,620 --> 00:13:36,960
Yes, unfortunately. Please take this to the general.

201
00:13:38,130 --> 00:13:41,330
Benedict is our finest journalist in Kigali, an expert on the subject.

202
00:13:43,040 --> 00:13:44,400
So what are you, Paul?

203
00:13:47,070 --> 00:13:48,300
I am Hutu.

204
00:13:49,210 --> 00:13:50,370
Gentlemen.

205
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:55,010
-More champagne? -More champagne would be nice.

206
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:58,380
Excuse me, honey. Can I ask you a personal question?

207
00:13:58,450 --> 00:14:02,890
-Are you a Hutu or a Tutsi? -I am Tutsi.

208
00:14:02,950 --> 00:14:06,790
-And your friend? Tutsi? -No, I am Hutu.

209
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:10,860
They could be twins.

210
00:14:11,430 --> 00:14:14,590
Get the camera. The general's going to give us an interview.

211
00:14:14,660 --> 00:14:15,650
Okay.

212
00:14:17,030 --> 00:14:20,940
I'm in room 22. I'd love to finish up this conversation.

213
00:14:23,810 --> 00:14:27,900
Senior U.N. Officers claim that the Rwandan army is secretly training

214
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:31,240
and arming the Hutu militia called the Interhamwe.

215
00:14:31,310 --> 00:14:35,760
I put this claim to the head of the armed forces, General Bizimungu.

216
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:39,520
No. No, we have not been training the militia.

217
00:14:39,590 --> 00:14:41,580
The U.N. Are mistaken in this accusation.

218
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:44,250
Do you support your president's agreement to make peace with the rebels?

219
00:14:44,330 --> 00:14:47,790
The president has the full support of the army.

220
00:14:47,860 --> 00:14:50,850
That peace agreement will be signed today in Tanzania

221
00:14:50,940 --> 00:14:54,310
between Tutsi rebel forces and President Habyarimana.

222
00:14:54,370 --> 00:14:57,170
This is a great day for Rwanda

223
00:14:57,240 --> 00:14:59,180
and for all of Africa.

224
00:14:59,240 --> 00:15:01,910
Negotiation has replaced confrontation...

225
00:15:01,980 --> 00:15:04,450
Paul, have a drink.

226
00:15:04,510 --> 00:15:06,350
Friendship has replaced fear.

227
00:15:06,410 --> 00:15:08,680
Ladies and gentlemen, we have a live feed

228
00:15:08,750 --> 00:15:10,610
to the signing of the peace agreement.

229
00:15:10,690 --> 00:15:14,150
To our president. May he find peace.

230
00:15:15,160 --> 00:15:16,890
May we all find peace.

231
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:22,660
Let us all dedicate ourselves to nurturing this hard-earned accord.

232
00:15:22,730 --> 00:15:23,990
To peace!

233
00:15:24,060 --> 00:15:25,190
Peace!

234
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:30,800
-Look me up if you come over. -Yes, it is a beautiful city.

235
00:15:30,870 --> 00:15:33,400
I am planning on returning there as... Forgive me.

236
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:35,570
-Thank you. Bye. -Thomas.

237
00:15:37,820 --> 00:15:39,670
-Hello, Fedens. -Paul.

238
00:15:40,250 --> 00:15:41,950
Well, this is a surprise.

239
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:44,420
Forgive us, Paul. We must talk.

240
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:47,250
Yes, what's wrong?

241
00:15:47,330 --> 00:15:50,150
I have it from a very reliable source, Paul.

242
00:15:50,230 --> 00:15:51,350
Who?

243
00:15:52,790 --> 00:15:54,260
Thank you, Sullivan.

244
00:15:56,170 --> 00:15:59,930
My assistant, the Hutu Power man.

245
00:16:00,010 --> 00:16:03,060
He says that we must get out now, that soon it'll be very bad.

246
00:16:04,240 --> 00:16:05,670
Give me this man's name.

247
00:16:05,740 --> 00:16:09,340
Please, Paul, even though he is Interhamwe, he's a friend.

248
00:16:09,410 --> 00:16:11,210
He wants your job, Thomas.

249
00:16:15,250 --> 00:16:18,480
He said that there is a signal.

250
00:16:19,650 --> 00:16:22,190
It is "Cut the tall trees. "

251
00:16:23,030 --> 00:16:26,020
And when they hear this signal, the militia are to go to war.

252
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:30,040
Paul, please, let us take Tatiana with us.

253
00:16:30,100 --> 00:16:32,070
You are Hutu. You will be safe.

254
00:16:33,270 --> 00:16:37,170
Fedens, I know you have heard many things.

255
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:40,130
And I know what we have seen, Thomas.

256
00:16:40,210 --> 00:16:42,940
But please, the United Nations are here now.

257
00:16:43,010 --> 00:16:45,570
The world press are watching.

258
00:16:45,650 --> 00:16:48,480
The peace has been signed. Let this process work...

259
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:50,110
What was that?

260
00:16:54,350 --> 00:16:55,690
Power cuts.

261
00:16:56,990 --> 00:16:59,190
We are running on generators.

262
00:17:00,190 --> 00:17:02,130
Fedens...

263
00:17:02,190 --> 00:17:03,820
Please, don't worry.

264
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:09,730
Tomorrow you will come by the house and we will discuss this with Tatiana.

265
00:17:09,810 --> 00:17:11,140
All right?

266
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:16,830
-Good night, Paul. -Yes. Kiss the girls for me.

267
00:17:45,340 --> 00:17:46,630
Shit!

268
00:18:00,790 --> 00:18:03,760
Stay in your houses. Stay in your house.

269
00:18:03,830 --> 00:18:05,960
Everybody stay in your house!

270
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:38,790
Tatiana?

271
00:19:08,700 --> 00:19:10,890
-Paul! -Tatiana!

272
00:19:12,490 --> 00:19:15,160
-What is going on here? -Our house has been burned.

273
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:18,070
-Didn't you hear the news? -What news?

274
00:19:18,130 --> 00:19:21,440
They are saying President Habyarimana has been murdered.

275
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:23,300
Tutsi rebels have killed him.

276
00:19:23,380 --> 00:19:26,830
Nonsense. Why would the rebels kill the president when he agreed to peace?

277
00:19:30,110 --> 00:19:32,840
Everyone, please, out of this room. Please.

278
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:34,910
Jean Baptiste, find them seats in the other room.

279
00:19:34,980 --> 00:19:36,790
Odette, please.

280
00:19:40,150 --> 00:19:44,280
-Did you meet with Thomas and Fedens? -Yes. I told them to go home.

281
00:19:45,290 --> 00:19:48,860
-Go and call them, Tatsi. -I've tried. Our phones, they do not work.

282
00:19:53,270 --> 00:19:57,230
-Why do the neighbors run to us? -You are the only Hutu they can trust.

283
00:19:57,310 --> 00:19:58,900
You are a Tutsi.

284
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:02,270
They are scared, Paul. I am scared.

285
00:20:08,590 --> 00:20:11,410
These are probably rumors started by agitators.

286
00:20:11,490 --> 00:20:14,320
We must remain calm for the children, Tatsi. We must.

287
00:20:14,820 --> 00:20:18,350
Forgive me, Paul. Elys says that Roger has gone.

288
00:20:18,430 --> 00:20:20,690
Gone? Gone where?

289
00:20:20,770 --> 00:20:24,460
-He was afraid for his friend Simon, Mama. -Where has he gone, Elys?

290
00:20:24,530 --> 00:20:25,660
He went next door.

291
00:20:26,570 --> 00:20:28,400
Wait. Paul!

292
00:20:28,470 --> 00:20:31,500
Tatiana, no. You have to stay here with the children.

293
00:20:31,570 --> 00:20:33,480
-Stay in the house. No! -Please.

294
00:20:41,350 --> 00:20:44,840
Paul, please, what is wrong? Tell me, what is wrong?

295
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:47,890
-Oh, my son! Where are you hurt? -Is he okay? Oh, my baby!

296
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:50,090
Talk to me. Where are you hurt?

297
00:20:50,160 --> 00:20:51,210
Paul?

298
00:20:53,860 --> 00:20:55,020
Oh, Tatsi.

299
00:20:57,400 --> 00:20:59,390
Odette, Odette!

300
00:20:59,470 --> 00:21:00,450
Oh, no.

301
00:21:00,540 --> 00:21:01,970
I'm okay.

302
00:21:02,040 --> 00:21:04,440
Get his clothes off. Tatsi, please get some water.

303
00:21:04,510 --> 00:21:06,740
-He's hurt. -Please, let's get his clothes off.

304
00:21:06,810 --> 00:21:09,210
-He's covered in blood. -Lay back, son.

305
00:21:10,980 --> 00:21:12,980
He went next door to the Chirangas.

306
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:15,610
Where is he hurt?

307
00:21:16,220 --> 00:21:18,270
Look here, Odette, look here.

308
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:20,980
Stay still, Roger. Keep him still, Paul.

309
00:21:21,830 --> 00:21:24,380
-I can't find the wound. -What happened to you?

310
00:21:24,460 --> 00:21:25,860
-Tell your mother. -Talk to me.

311
00:21:25,930 --> 00:21:28,090
Tell your mother what happened, Roger.

312
00:21:28,170 --> 00:21:29,600
Roger, you're okay.

313
00:21:29,670 --> 00:21:33,430
Do not worry, he is not cut. He is not hurt.

314
00:21:33,510 --> 00:21:35,940
This is not his blood, Paul.

315
00:21:37,270 --> 00:21:38,610
You are not hurt.

316
00:21:38,680 --> 00:21:42,130
My darling, it's okay. It's okay.

317
00:21:42,210 --> 00:21:44,080
You are safe. Look at your mother.

318
00:21:44,140 --> 00:21:46,210
Come here, Elys.

319
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:49,770
-Where did the blood come from? -Please, please!

320
00:21:50,690 --> 00:21:52,620
-You are safe. -You are out, Roger.

321
00:21:52,690 --> 00:21:55,410
You are safe, you are safe, Roger. You are safe, Roger.

322
00:21:55,490 --> 00:21:57,190
It's okay.

323
00:21:57,260 --> 00:21:59,420
I love you so much. I love you.

324
00:22:19,310 --> 00:22:20,580
Oh, son.

325
00:22:25,090 --> 00:22:26,490
Paul.

326
00:22:26,560 --> 00:22:32,090
Listen to me, good people of Rwanda. Terrible news...

327
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:35,150
-It is true. -Horrible news...

328
00:22:35,240 --> 00:22:39,930
Our great president is murdered by the Tutsi cockroaches.

329
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:40,990
Oh, my God!

330
00:22:41,070 --> 00:22:44,900
They tricked him to sign their phony peace agreement.

331
00:22:44,970 --> 00:22:47,600
Then they shot his plane from the sky.

332
00:22:48,580 --> 00:22:52,950
It is time to clear the brush, good Hutus of Rwanda.

333
00:22:54,050 --> 00:22:56,880
We must cut the tall trees.

334
00:22:57,550 --> 00:23:00,390
Cut the tall trees now!

335
00:23:00,460 --> 00:23:01,950
The soldiers are here!

336
00:23:02,020 --> 00:23:04,990
-Let us go to work, loyal Hutus. -No, no.

337
00:23:05,060 --> 00:23:07,620
Everyone, stay calm. Stay calm and be quiet.

338
00:23:07,700 --> 00:23:12,160
Find these traitors. Let none of them escape.

339
00:23:13,070 --> 00:23:15,800
Split up. Everybody out.

340
00:23:17,900 --> 00:23:20,370
-You two, check the back. -Go.

341
00:23:22,120 --> 00:23:24,480
-You, go and find him. -Yes, sir.

342
00:23:30,750 --> 00:23:32,720
I better go have a word with them.

343
00:23:34,130 --> 00:23:36,790
Go around the back. Make sure no one comes out.

344
00:23:36,860 --> 00:23:37,880
Yes, sir!

345
00:23:39,470 --> 00:23:41,660
Who's in charge here?

346
00:23:41,730 --> 00:23:42,890
You.

347
00:23:48,840 --> 00:23:51,740
-Can I help you, sir? -Everybody out! Out!

348
00:23:51,810 --> 00:23:54,710
-Let me see your identity card. -Grab your things. Go!

349
00:23:54,770 --> 00:23:56,840
I am a good friend of General Bizimungu.

350
00:23:56,910 --> 00:23:58,010
Get out!

351
00:24:01,610 --> 00:24:03,520
Get out of here!

352
00:24:03,580 --> 00:24:05,980
Everybody, out! Get out, get out!

353
00:24:06,060 --> 00:24:07,580
You work at the Hotel Diplomat?

354
00:24:09,190 --> 00:24:10,930
No, I work at the Mille Collines.

355
00:24:12,590 --> 00:24:14,430
I used to work at the Diplomat.

356
00:24:14,500 --> 00:24:17,220
We want to use that hotel. All the room keys are in the safe.

357
00:24:17,300 --> 00:24:19,740
You must open it. Let's go.

358
00:24:19,800 --> 00:24:23,360
-Paul! -Sir, I cannot leave my family.

359
00:24:23,440 --> 00:24:26,140
I must take them with me. It is not safe here.

360
00:24:26,210 --> 00:24:28,400
There are Tutsi spies everywhere.

361
00:24:28,470 --> 00:24:30,100
I cannot take all these people.

362
00:24:30,180 --> 00:24:32,180
No, no, sir, you do not have to.

363
00:24:32,250 --> 00:24:35,040
We have our car and our van.

364
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:37,820
-Captain Kaliso, come on. -Roger.

365
00:24:38,320 --> 00:24:42,350
-Let's go! -Come on. Hurry! Go around, go around.

366
00:24:42,430 --> 00:24:44,720
We found him. Let's go. Let's go!

367
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:49,490
-Can I go with you? -Yes, of course, Jeremiah. Hurry.

368
00:24:59,810 --> 00:25:01,330
Oh, Jesus, no!

369
00:25:03,280 --> 00:25:04,770
Oh, it's Simon, Papa!

370
00:25:05,890 --> 00:25:09,050
Don't look, don't look, don't look. Don't look, Tatiana.

371
00:26:13,450 --> 00:26:16,350
-The safe is in the manager's office. -You two, go with him.

372
00:26:24,690 --> 00:26:27,060
Look at this. Beer.

373
00:26:44,210 --> 00:26:45,480
I've got them.

374
00:26:57,160 --> 00:26:58,640
Get down, all of you!

375
00:27:04,570 --> 00:27:08,560
Sir, sir. Here, I have them. I have them. I've got them.

376
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:15,080
Traitor!

377
00:27:15,140 --> 00:27:17,110
These are Tutsi cockroaches!

378
00:27:17,780 --> 00:27:20,220
Let me explain, sir. Please wait.

379
00:27:23,520 --> 00:27:24,680
Shoot them.

380
00:27:26,060 --> 00:27:27,290
Shoot them.

381
00:27:29,120 --> 00:27:32,720
Please, I don't use guns. I don't.

382
00:27:32,790 --> 00:27:33,780
It's easy.

383
00:27:38,770 --> 00:27:42,110
Shoot them, or you die first.

384
00:27:42,970 --> 00:27:46,700
Sir, what could I pay you not to do this?

385
00:27:46,780 --> 00:27:48,610
You wanna pay me?

386
00:27:48,670 --> 00:27:51,080
Why not? Look at them.

387
00:27:51,150 --> 00:27:52,940
These are not rebels.

388
00:27:53,950 --> 00:27:55,520
Soon they will be worthless to you.

389
00:27:55,520 --> 00:27:57,410
Why not take some money for your work?

390
00:27:57,480 --> 00:28:00,110
-How much? -You name a price.

391
00:28:07,930 --> 00:28:09,700
10,000 francs for each.

392
00:28:10,600 --> 00:28:13,260
-Sir, I don't have that much. -Okay.

393
00:28:13,330 --> 00:28:15,300
Wait, wait! Here.

394
00:28:15,370 --> 00:28:18,810
It's 1,000 U.S. And here.

395
00:28:19,510 --> 00:28:22,340
50,000 francs for my wife and children.

396
00:28:22,420 --> 00:28:24,640
-Take them. -Go, go, go.

397
00:28:24,710 --> 00:28:27,120
Go, go, go.

398
00:28:27,180 --> 00:28:29,080
-Have you any money? -Nothing.

399
00:28:29,150 --> 00:28:32,380
-Paul, don't let them die. -Get in the van.

400
00:28:37,460 --> 00:28:40,290
Sir, I have more money actually.

401
00:28:42,230 --> 00:28:45,530
And let them give you something. Some money, whatever they have.

402
00:28:45,610 --> 00:28:46,760
All right?

403
00:28:48,280 --> 00:28:50,470
Here you are. Give me everything you have.

404
00:28:52,640 --> 00:28:54,470
Here, Paul, it's all I have.

405
00:28:57,450 --> 00:28:59,640
Here you are. See?

406
00:29:01,550 --> 00:29:04,540
This is enough for one cockroach. Pick one.

407
00:29:06,190 --> 00:29:07,350
Sir...

408
00:29:09,530 --> 00:29:12,860
I will give you 100,000 francs for all of them.

409
00:29:14,860 --> 00:29:16,790
-Give me it. -I don't have it here.

410
00:29:16,870 --> 00:29:18,860
At the Mille Collines I can get it for you.

411
00:29:18,930 --> 00:29:21,400
You'll run into the hotel and hide behind the U.N.

412
00:29:21,480 --> 00:29:26,140
Sir, I swear. 100,000 francs.

413
00:29:26,210 --> 00:29:29,730
I will get you the money. You keep them outside.

414
00:29:32,350 --> 00:29:34,510
Please, sir. Please.

415
00:29:35,920 --> 00:29:38,410
-Let's go. -Okay. Everyone in the van.

416
00:29:38,490 --> 00:29:40,290
Come on now. Hurry.

417
00:29:52,010 --> 00:29:55,800
Go with my soldiers. And hurry back if you want to keep these cockroaches.

418
00:30:00,440 --> 00:30:03,200
The soldiers are here. Where is the car?

419
00:30:03,280 --> 00:30:06,610
There is nothing I can do. Excuse me, sir! Please, could you...

420
00:30:18,990 --> 00:30:20,330
Here's the money.

421
00:30:20,400 --> 00:30:22,890
100,000 francs as promised.

422
00:30:22,960 --> 00:30:24,930
Now please, let them go, sir.

423
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:27,230
Take the money. We will get them later.

424
00:30:30,110 --> 00:30:32,260
-You can go. -Thank you.

425
00:30:34,310 --> 00:30:35,470
Traitor.

426
00:30:40,090 --> 00:30:41,350
Thank you, Paul.

427
00:30:46,820 --> 00:30:49,690
Do you understand, Dube? Because I can't wait for Paul.

428
00:30:49,760 --> 00:30:52,130
-You must tell him when he comes... -Here he is, sir.

429
00:30:53,630 --> 00:30:57,690
Paul, I have to go. The staff of Kivu Lodge have fled.

430
00:30:57,770 --> 00:31:00,740
I have to close up there. You are in charge now.

431
00:31:00,800 --> 00:31:01,930
It's okay, it's okay.

432
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:05,770
There were no survivors in last night's plane crash in Kigali, Rwanda.

433
00:31:05,840 --> 00:31:08,680
Everyone, please move to the side. Clear the door.

434
00:31:08,750 --> 00:31:10,070
Come, Tatsi.

435
00:31:12,420 --> 00:31:14,640
Andre, I need two suites.

436
00:31:14,710 --> 00:31:17,020
-Paul, please, where is my passport? -Yes, I understand.

437
00:31:17,090 --> 00:31:21,280
-I need to get hold of my embassy. -If you give me one moment, please.

438
00:31:22,660 --> 00:31:26,320
-Odette, Jean Baptiste, take this room. -What about our neighbors?

439
00:31:27,560 --> 00:31:29,050
What will they do?

440
00:31:31,640 --> 00:31:33,960
-Dube. -Yes, sir?

441
00:31:35,670 --> 00:31:40,010
Please... put these "guests" in two staff rooms.

442
00:31:40,070 --> 00:31:41,540
Right away, sir.

443
00:31:50,290 --> 00:31:53,380
No, no, no. Please, it's old. Have the fruit.

444
00:31:57,300 --> 00:31:59,960
It's all right, Roger. It's all right. We're here.

445
00:32:01,230 --> 00:32:02,890
-Ah, Joseph. -Your suit, sir.

446
00:32:02,970 --> 00:32:04,330
This mess is unacceptable.

447
00:32:04,400 --> 00:32:07,460
Call housekeeping, get them up here right away. Thank you.

448
00:32:09,510 --> 00:32:11,770
-I'm trying Thomas and Fedens. -All right.

449
00:32:14,480 --> 00:32:16,960
Operator, I need a line.

450
00:32:17,050 --> 00:32:19,910
I need a line now. Please. Hello?

451
00:32:24,720 --> 00:32:26,880
You did not reach them?

452
00:32:26,950 --> 00:32:29,150
No. No answer.

453
00:32:30,660 --> 00:32:34,320
It is a very tense situation, and I just want to assure the families

454
00:32:34,400 --> 00:32:37,530
of those who are there that we are doing everything we possibly can

455
00:32:37,600 --> 00:32:40,160
to try to ensure the safety of our citizens there.

456
00:32:40,240 --> 00:32:42,470
Can you at least tell us, is the airport actually open?

457
00:32:42,540 --> 00:32:45,230
We are calling the airport. We are calling the embassy.

458
00:32:45,300 --> 00:32:47,870
We are trying to get as much information for you as we can.

459
00:32:47,940 --> 00:32:49,840
-And yes, your passport, yes. -And my passport.

460
00:32:49,910 --> 00:32:52,250
Antoinette will take care of this for you.

461
00:32:54,110 --> 00:32:56,510
Dube, where is Gregoire?

462
00:32:58,980 --> 00:33:02,390
Sir, he has moved into the Presidential Suite.

463
00:33:17,080 --> 00:33:18,230
Mr. Manager.

464
00:33:20,140 --> 00:33:22,210
What do you think you are doing, Gregoire?

465
00:33:22,280 --> 00:33:23,640
Who is it?

466
00:33:24,380 --> 00:33:25,840
It's okay, darling.

467
00:33:26,650 --> 00:33:27,980
What do you want?

468
00:33:28,060 --> 00:33:31,580
You had better get out of this room and back downstairs right away.

469
00:33:31,650 --> 00:33:34,920
-I don't have to listen to you anymore. -Yes, you do.

470
00:33:34,990 --> 00:33:38,190
I am in charge. Now get out of this room right now.

471
00:33:44,240 --> 00:33:48,830
Mr. Manager, do you notice the smell of cockroaches?

472
00:33:50,340 --> 00:33:53,400
If I were to leave this room, I'm sure I could find it.

473
00:33:54,180 --> 00:33:56,670
And I know people who can cleanse it.

474
00:33:57,910 --> 00:34:01,640
But maybe it doesn't bother you. Why is that?

475
00:34:03,020 --> 00:34:04,850
Are you used to the smell?

476
00:34:06,430 --> 00:34:07,750
Well, not me.

477
00:34:08,760 --> 00:34:11,090
I need a clean room to escape it.

478
00:34:17,360 --> 00:34:21,130
Please move into the hotel. Everyone, keep moving.

479
00:34:21,200 --> 00:34:23,500
My house has been burned. I have nowhere to go.

480
00:34:23,570 --> 00:34:25,160
Yes, I understand this, Your Honor.

481
00:34:25,240 --> 00:34:27,470
But we are operating at capacity as it is.

482
00:34:27,540 --> 00:34:31,380
I can give you one room, but you will have to share it. I'm sorry.

483
00:34:31,450 --> 00:34:34,080
-There's no way we can share. -I am sorry. Forgive me.

484
00:34:34,150 --> 00:34:35,610
There are eight of us.

485
00:34:35,690 --> 00:34:37,240
-Yes? -Paul, I need your help.

486
00:34:37,320 --> 00:34:38,480
Yes, Madame Archer.

487
00:34:45,920 --> 00:34:48,790
They're Tutsi children from the St. Francis orphanage.

488
00:34:49,370 --> 00:34:51,020
Okay, come on, let's go.

489
00:34:51,700 --> 00:34:54,570
-I have only one room. -That'll do.

490
00:34:56,900 --> 00:34:58,340
Come.

491
00:34:58,410 --> 00:35:00,800
-Otto, please. -Excuse me.

492
00:35:01,880 --> 00:35:04,850
Corporal, take that lady's bag, please, and quickly.

493
00:35:07,550 --> 00:35:10,950
-Have to go get the rest of them. -The rest of them?

494
00:35:11,020 --> 00:35:13,390
There are another ten. I'll be back soon.

495
00:35:15,950 --> 00:35:17,890
Madame Archer.

496
00:35:17,960 --> 00:35:19,720
I have a favor to ask of you.

497
00:35:19,790 --> 00:35:23,330
My brother-in-law and his family, they live near the St. Francis.

498
00:35:23,400 --> 00:35:25,500
On O'Clare, 20.

499
00:35:25,570 --> 00:35:28,560
Can you please get them and bring them here to me?

500
00:35:28,630 --> 00:35:30,660
-Sure. -And I have a photo.

501
00:35:32,680 --> 00:35:34,370
Please, keep moving!

502
00:35:38,080 --> 00:35:39,740
-Thanks, Paul. -Thank you.

503
00:35:39,810 --> 00:35:41,680
Please move into the hotel!

504
00:35:41,750 --> 00:35:43,380
Come on, kids, don't be afraid.

505
00:35:43,450 --> 00:35:46,150
-Take them around the back. -Everyone, keep moving!

506
00:35:52,060 --> 00:35:54,460
Has he spoken to you yet?

507
00:35:54,530 --> 00:35:55,520
No.

508
00:36:09,280 --> 00:36:11,300
Is your face still hurting?

509
00:36:12,340 --> 00:36:13,510
It's all right.

510
00:36:20,050 --> 00:36:22,780
The neighbors asked me to thank you for your kindness.

511
00:36:25,520 --> 00:36:27,590
I shouldn't have brought them here.

512
00:36:29,600 --> 00:36:32,930
The first thing they told me when I received my appointment

513
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:35,840
was to never, never lower the tone of the hotel.

514
00:36:37,230 --> 00:36:40,140
"Maintain the Mille Collines' dignity at all times, Paul. "

515
00:36:44,950 --> 00:36:46,940
Soon all of this will be over.

516
00:36:49,450 --> 00:36:51,610
What if I lose my job, Tatsi?

517
00:36:54,600 --> 00:36:55,650
Oh, my God!

518
00:36:55,720 --> 00:36:57,920
-Where are you going? -I'll be right back.

519
00:37:18,010 --> 00:37:19,940
Take care of them.

520
00:37:20,020 --> 00:37:21,350
How, sir?

521
00:37:22,690 --> 00:37:25,180
Bathe them, feed them.

522
00:37:26,690 --> 00:37:28,020
Put them to bed.

523
00:37:31,120 --> 00:37:32,790
I will send you some help.

524
00:37:37,670 --> 00:37:39,390
Okay, babies.

525
00:37:39,730 --> 00:37:42,000
We have heard reports of reprisal massacres.

526
00:37:42,070 --> 00:37:44,560
Will the U.N. Intervene to stop the bloodshed?

527
00:37:44,650 --> 00:37:47,770
We're here as peacekeepers, not as peacemakers.

528
00:37:47,850 --> 00:37:50,470
My orders are not to intervene.

529
00:37:51,440 --> 00:37:53,350
-Excuse me. -Thank you, Colonel.

530
00:37:54,050 --> 00:37:55,150
Here. Over here.

531
00:37:55,220 --> 00:37:58,350
Listen, I got us a car, but we gotta move now.

532
00:37:59,090 --> 00:38:00,680
We're not allowed to do that, Jack.

533
00:38:00,750 --> 00:38:04,150
David, the shit's going down outside these walls. We gotta cover it.

534
00:38:04,230 --> 00:38:07,360
We're not leaving the hotel grounds unless we have an armored car.

535
00:38:07,430 --> 00:38:09,590
-That's the ground rules. -The ground rules?

536
00:38:09,670 --> 00:38:11,490
Where do you think we are, fucking Wimbledon?

537
00:38:11,570 --> 00:38:16,560
We cover the story from here until we get the proper vehicles, Jack.

538
00:38:16,640 --> 00:38:19,080
Shoot some "B" roll of the refugees.

539
00:38:24,780 --> 00:38:26,010
Let's go.

540
00:38:26,080 --> 00:38:28,710
Colonel, I have no way to protect these people.

541
00:38:28,780 --> 00:38:31,650
And I have more refugees than I have room for as it is.

542
00:38:31,720 --> 00:38:35,150
I was given 20 orphans today by the Red Cross.

543
00:38:35,230 --> 00:38:37,280
This is not a refugee camp.

544
00:38:37,350 --> 00:38:39,550
Can you not take them with you to your facilities?

545
00:38:39,630 --> 00:38:42,890
No, I can't do that, Paul. I'm sorry.

546
00:38:43,800 --> 00:38:46,530
I'm overwhelmed at my refugee camp.

547
00:38:46,600 --> 00:38:49,200
I'm under attack, constant attack.

548
00:38:49,270 --> 00:38:53,170
As soon as we can stabilize this situation, then I'll take 'em.

549
00:38:56,110 --> 00:39:00,810
...and stop the Tutsi cockroaches who try to run from justice.

550
00:39:00,890 --> 00:39:05,410
The Tutsi cockroach judge called Makesa is hiding at 4...

551
00:39:08,050 --> 00:39:12,390
-... Kabulla and his cockroaches... -Turn that radio off.

552
00:39:13,190 --> 00:39:14,890
Watch out for him. He...

553
00:39:17,300 --> 00:39:21,060
And get back to work. We have a hotel to run.

554
00:39:21,140 --> 00:39:24,330
There's no work here anyway. The boss has left.

555
00:39:24,400 --> 00:39:26,100
I am your boss!

556
00:39:39,520 --> 00:39:43,510
Sir, there's a call from the Mille Collines in Rwanda on line one.

557
00:39:43,590 --> 00:39:46,150
Yes? Who am I speaking to?

558
00:39:46,860 --> 00:39:50,430
Yes, sir, Paul Rusesabagina, the house manager.

559
00:39:50,500 --> 00:39:52,600
I met you on your last visit here, Mr. Tillens.

560
00:39:52,670 --> 00:39:55,430
Ah, yes. Paul, I remember.

561
00:39:55,510 --> 00:39:57,270
How are things there?

562
00:39:57,340 --> 00:39:59,630
The situation is difficult, sir.

563
00:40:01,010 --> 00:40:05,170
Some of our directors believe we should close the Mille Collines

564
00:40:05,240 --> 00:40:07,270
until this unrest is over.

565
00:40:07,350 --> 00:40:10,980
I'm not sure about that, Paul. What do you think?

566
00:40:13,490 --> 00:40:17,710
Sir, that would be very bad for our reputation.

567
00:40:17,790 --> 00:40:22,060
The Mille Collines is an oasis of calm for all our loyal customers.

568
00:40:22,130 --> 00:40:25,360
What would they think if Sabena deserted them now?

569
00:40:25,430 --> 00:40:28,530
I assure you, the United Nations have everything under control, sir.

570
00:40:30,040 --> 00:40:31,940
Very well, Paul. Very well.

571
00:40:32,010 --> 00:40:35,940
But if this thing gets worse, we must close.

572
00:40:36,010 --> 00:40:39,310
If there is anything I can do, please call.

573
00:40:39,950 --> 00:40:43,440
Sir, yes, there is one thing I'm going to be needing from you right away.

574
00:40:44,780 --> 00:40:48,380
Let me tell you, it was an embarrassment for me to have to ask for this.

575
00:40:49,190 --> 00:40:53,350
Most of us in this room have known each other and worked together for many years.

576
00:40:54,490 --> 00:40:58,480
Is it really necessary for me to get a letter from Belgium

577
00:40:58,570 --> 00:41:00,300
for you to perform your duties?

578
00:41:04,880 --> 00:41:07,870
In fact, forget this letter.

579
00:41:07,940 --> 00:41:12,010
If you don't want to work for me and would rather be out there, then leave now.

580
00:41:17,250 --> 00:41:20,850
Please, everyone, back to work.

581
00:41:26,630 --> 00:41:28,690
Paul, thank you for coming.

582
00:41:28,770 --> 00:41:32,290
The air conditioner's on the blink. Is there any way you can have a look at it?

583
00:41:32,360 --> 00:41:34,230
-I'm just on a deadline. -Certainly.

584
00:41:34,300 --> 00:41:38,500
Fred, let me know when you get the satellite feed. Thanks.

585
00:41:39,110 --> 00:41:43,070
Mr. Fleming, I brought you some tea as well, sir.

586
00:41:43,140 --> 00:41:44,580
Thank you, Paul.

587
00:41:45,840 --> 00:41:48,150
You're an oasis in the desert.

588
00:41:49,550 --> 00:41:51,720
...the elements of the government and army

589
00:41:51,790 --> 00:41:55,520
are following the example of what happened to the Americans in Somalia.

590
00:41:55,590 --> 00:42:01,460
I think they intend to intimidate us, try to attack us, and...

591
00:42:01,530 --> 00:42:05,160
hope that the West will pull all its troops out.

592
00:42:05,230 --> 00:42:07,640
-Do you think they'll succeed? -No, they won't.

593
00:42:07,700 --> 00:42:09,100
The U.N.'s here to stay.

594
00:42:09,170 --> 00:42:10,830
What about the outbreak of violence

595
00:42:10,900 --> 00:42:12,870
since the shooting down of the president's plane?

596
00:42:12,940 --> 00:42:15,740
What the hell do you think you're doing?

597
00:42:15,810 --> 00:42:18,870
I'm responsible for the safety of this crew.

598
00:42:21,450 --> 00:42:22,750
What is this?

599
00:42:52,850 --> 00:42:55,690
-Where did you get this? -Half a mile down the road.

600
00:42:56,280 --> 00:42:58,080
Fred, it's David.

601
00:42:58,160 --> 00:43:00,980
I've got incredible footage. It's a massacre.

602
00:43:01,060 --> 00:43:03,760
Dead bodies, machetes.

603
00:43:03,830 --> 00:43:06,960
If I get this through right away, can you make the evening news?

604
00:43:07,930 --> 00:43:09,020
Yeah.

605
00:43:14,300 --> 00:43:16,000
You have to lead with this.

606
00:43:17,240 --> 00:43:19,300
I point at you, you do a shot.

607
00:43:19,380 --> 00:43:23,370
And you'll get a total double and see if all the drinking...

608
00:43:23,440 --> 00:43:25,470
-Excuse me, Mr. Daglish. -Hey, Paul.

609
00:43:26,250 --> 00:43:29,310
Listen, sorry about earlier.

610
00:43:29,390 --> 00:43:32,010
If I'd known you were in there, I wouldn't have...

611
00:43:32,090 --> 00:43:36,890
I am glad that you have shot this footage and that the world will see it.

612
00:43:36,960 --> 00:43:40,050
It is the only way we have a chance that people might intervene.

613
00:43:43,330 --> 00:43:47,660
Yeah, and if no one intervenes, is it still a good thing to show?

614
00:43:49,440 --> 00:43:53,380
How can they not intervene when they witness such atrocities?

615
00:43:53,440 --> 00:43:57,810
I think if people see this footage...

616
00:43:58,920 --> 00:44:01,510
...they'll say, "Oh, my God, that's horrible,"

617
00:44:01,580 --> 00:44:03,410
and then go on eating their dinners.

618
00:44:08,150 --> 00:44:11,320
What the hell do I know? Listen, you wanna just relax?

619
00:44:11,400 --> 00:44:14,060
I have more work to do. I thank you for your offer.

620
00:44:14,130 --> 00:44:16,360
Please enjoy your evening, Mr. Daglish.

621
00:44:20,410 --> 00:44:23,340
-Help! Please help us! Please! -Sir! Sir!

622
00:44:23,410 --> 00:44:25,430
We've got trouble at the gate.

623
00:44:28,170 --> 00:44:30,800
Can we have some medical assistance here, please?

624
00:44:30,870 --> 00:44:34,080
That group, come with me. Move out of the area.

625
00:44:34,150 --> 00:44:36,380
-Here, get up, get up. -Right, fall back, everybody.

626
00:44:37,480 --> 00:44:39,480
Benedict, what is happening?

627
00:44:39,550 --> 00:44:42,490
They're killing everyone. The lady...

628
00:44:42,550 --> 00:44:45,330
The Interhamwe have surrounded the whole town.

629
00:44:45,390 --> 00:44:46,560
Come on!

630
00:44:47,100 --> 00:44:49,090
Cover the road. Now.

631
00:44:49,970 --> 00:44:51,520
Stand your ground.

632
00:44:53,440 --> 00:44:54,490
Hold the line.

633
00:44:54,560 --> 00:44:56,930
Do not shoot! Do not shoot!

634
00:45:23,470 --> 00:45:26,130
-Lieutenant, guard this gate. -Yes, sir.

635
00:45:26,640 --> 00:45:29,600
You two, take up positions behind those sandbags.

636
00:45:29,670 --> 00:45:34,830
They murdered my men. I lost ten Belgian U.N. Soldiers.

637
00:45:34,910 --> 00:45:37,350
They were protecting the lady prime minister.

638
00:45:37,410 --> 00:45:39,540
-She is dead? -Yeah, she's dead.

639
00:45:40,940 --> 00:45:44,540
The Europeans are putting together an intervention force.

640
00:45:44,610 --> 00:45:46,110
They'll be here in a few days.

641
00:45:46,190 --> 00:45:49,880
I understand that, Colonel, but there is simply no place for me to put all of them.

642
00:45:49,950 --> 00:45:51,320
What can I do?

643
00:45:51,390 --> 00:45:54,760
I'll put two more men on the gate, two of my best lieutenants.

644
00:45:55,590 --> 00:45:56,990
-All right. -All right.

645
00:45:57,060 --> 00:45:58,860
I understand. Thank you.

646
00:46:08,680 --> 00:46:09,940
Madame Archer.

647
00:46:11,210 --> 00:46:12,310
Hello.

648
00:46:13,450 --> 00:46:16,620
-We were expecting you five days ago. -I'm sorry.

649
00:46:16,690 --> 00:46:19,180
My brother and his family, did you find them?

650
00:46:19,250 --> 00:46:21,990
I made it to the house, but it was empty.

651
00:46:22,060 --> 00:46:24,610
-Empty? -It had been ransacked.

652
00:46:25,860 --> 00:46:29,020
As I left, an old woman, she waved to me.

653
00:46:29,100 --> 00:46:33,120
I went to the house. She has the two little girls. They're safe.

654
00:46:33,200 --> 00:46:34,760
Okay.

655
00:46:34,830 --> 00:46:36,600
But...

656
00:46:36,670 --> 00:46:41,080
My brother and his wife... did the old lady know of them?

657
00:46:44,280 --> 00:46:48,220
My brother is dead. They would never leave their children.

658
00:46:48,280 --> 00:46:51,810
Perhaps they could not make it home, Tatiana. They are hiding.

659
00:46:53,350 --> 00:46:56,380
Please, can you return and bring the girls back here to us?

660
00:46:56,460 --> 00:47:00,190
I can't. There are Interhamwe roadblocks everywhere.

661
00:47:03,930 --> 00:47:05,930
When I reached the orphanage...

662
00:47:07,200 --> 00:47:09,140
...the Interhamwe were there.

663
00:47:10,110 --> 00:47:12,940
They'd already started killing children.

664
00:47:13,670 --> 00:47:15,340
They made me watch.

665
00:47:18,280 --> 00:47:20,270
There was one girl,

666
00:47:20,350 --> 00:47:22,970
she had her little sister wrapped on her back.

667
00:47:26,850 --> 00:47:29,950
As they were about to chop her, she cried out to me.

668
00:47:32,460 --> 00:47:34,450
"Please don't let them kill me.

669
00:47:35,730 --> 00:47:38,400
I promise I won't be Tutsi anymore. "

670
00:47:38,470 --> 00:47:41,230
Please, I can't.

671
00:47:48,610 --> 00:47:52,770
They're targeting Tutsi children, Paul, to wipe out the next generation.

672
00:48:01,190 --> 00:48:04,350
I've nowhere to take the orphans, Paul.

673
00:48:04,420 --> 00:48:08,880
Don't worry. There will be an intervention force coming soon.

674
00:48:09,930 --> 00:48:12,050
We will get the orphans out then.

675
00:48:25,050 --> 00:48:26,310
They're here!

676
00:48:32,190 --> 00:48:35,060
They're here! We are safe!

677
00:48:35,120 --> 00:48:36,450
Soldiers have arrived!

678
00:48:37,060 --> 00:48:39,720
-Wow, look, it's the French! -Yes!

679
00:48:39,790 --> 00:48:41,620
Thank goodness!

680
00:48:43,130 --> 00:48:45,070
-Welcome. -Thank you.

681
00:48:45,130 --> 00:48:46,300
Well done.

682
00:48:49,740 --> 00:48:51,210
About time, gentlemen.

683
00:48:52,510 --> 00:48:54,410
Thank you for saving our lives.

684
00:48:58,710 --> 00:48:59,980
It's okay, Roger.

685
00:49:02,250 --> 00:49:06,090
Jean Baptiste, our prayers have been answered. Thank God.

686
00:49:06,150 --> 00:49:07,920
Yes, finally!

687
00:49:10,200 --> 00:49:11,590
See, it's okay.

688
00:49:13,930 --> 00:49:16,160
We can do nothing from our side.

689
00:49:19,370 --> 00:49:22,030
Sweetheart, I told you we'd be safe.

690
00:49:22,100 --> 00:49:24,900
See? I told you. Yeah.

691
00:49:26,910 --> 00:49:30,170
So, Colonel, what can I get for you?

692
00:49:32,380 --> 00:49:33,540
Something strong.

693
00:49:34,250 --> 00:49:35,620
-Scotch? -Yeah.

694
00:49:38,890 --> 00:49:40,650
Congratulations, Colonel.

695
00:49:41,920 --> 00:49:43,980
You have performed a minor miracle.

696
00:49:46,190 --> 00:49:48,920
-Congratulations, huh? -Yes, sir.

697
00:49:52,400 --> 00:49:54,330
You should spit in my face.

698
00:49:56,110 --> 00:49:57,730
Excuse me, Colonel?

699
00:49:57,810 --> 00:49:59,600
You're dirt.

700
00:50:02,340 --> 00:50:03,740
We think you're dirt, Paul.

701
00:50:05,340 --> 00:50:06,740
Who is "we"?

702
00:50:07,780 --> 00:50:11,110
The West, all the superpowers, everything you believe in, Paul.

703
00:50:11,180 --> 00:50:14,420
They think you're dirt, they think you're dung. You're worthless.

704
00:50:14,490 --> 00:50:17,010
I'm afraid I don't understand what you are saying, sir.

705
00:50:17,100 --> 00:50:19,390
Come on, don't bullshit me, Paul.

706
00:50:20,390 --> 00:50:22,230
You're the smartest man here.

707
00:50:23,200 --> 00:50:26,260
You got them all eating out of your hands.

708
00:50:26,330 --> 00:50:30,230
You could own this freakin' hotel, except for one thing...

709
00:50:30,310 --> 00:50:31,630
you're black.

710
00:50:33,210 --> 00:50:35,200
You're not even a nigger.

711
00:50:36,480 --> 00:50:38,070
You're an African.

712
00:50:43,650 --> 00:50:45,520
They're not gonna stay, Paul.

713
00:50:47,390 --> 00:50:49,540
They're not gonna stop this slaughter.

714
00:50:52,060 --> 00:50:53,180
Please.

715
00:50:53,860 --> 00:50:54,960
Got it.

716
00:50:57,060 --> 00:50:59,130
-Hello. -Hello, Daddy.

717
00:51:00,640 --> 00:51:03,070
Elys, take Diane in the other room.

718
00:51:06,810 --> 00:51:08,530
What is it?

719
00:51:14,020 --> 00:51:15,670
All the whites are leaving.

720
00:51:16,750 --> 00:51:18,550
They are being evacuated.

721
00:51:19,660 --> 00:51:22,480
But... what about us?

722
00:51:23,190 --> 00:51:25,120
We have been abandoned.

723
00:51:25,190 --> 00:51:28,190
But the soldiers will stop the killers.

724
00:51:28,260 --> 00:51:30,700
Listen. Listen to me, Tatsi. Listen.

725
00:51:30,760 --> 00:51:34,000
I said all the whites are leaving... the French, the Italians,

726
00:51:34,070 --> 00:51:36,660
even the U.N. Belgian soldiers, all of them!

727
00:51:39,410 --> 00:51:41,340
Who is left?

728
00:51:42,240 --> 00:51:43,610
I don't know.

729
00:51:44,810 --> 00:51:50,480
Colonel Oliver said he has 300 U.N. Peacekeepers for the whole country.

730
00:51:52,920 --> 00:51:55,580
The most he can spare for the hotel are four men.

731
00:51:56,820 --> 00:51:59,020
And they are not allowed to shoot.

732
00:52:04,870 --> 00:52:06,690
I am a fool.

733
00:52:06,770 --> 00:52:08,970
No. No, no.

734
00:52:09,770 --> 00:52:12,710
They told me I was one of them, and I...

735
00:52:15,470 --> 00:52:19,970
Wine, chocolates, cigars, style... I swallowed it.

736
00:52:20,050 --> 00:52:22,310
I swallowed it. I swallowed all of it.

737
00:52:23,720 --> 00:52:25,680
And they handed me their shit.

738
00:52:30,660 --> 00:52:34,150
I have no history. I have no memory.

739
00:52:35,800 --> 00:52:37,740
I'm a fool, Tatsi.

740
00:52:39,400 --> 00:52:41,460
You are no fool.

741
00:52:44,970 --> 00:52:47,100
I know who you are.

742
00:52:50,950 --> 00:52:52,530
News Service Africa.

743
00:52:52,620 --> 00:52:56,350
A United Nations source reports that the U.S. And British representatives

744
00:52:56,420 --> 00:52:59,050
on the Security Council will lobby for the removal

745
00:52:59,120 --> 00:53:01,720
of all U.N. Peacekeepers from Rwanda.

746
00:53:22,740 --> 00:53:24,210
Please, Jack. Please don't go.

747
00:53:24,280 --> 00:53:26,210
Wait, he's British. Take out your passport.

748
00:53:27,120 --> 00:53:28,940
Jack, please don't leave me.

749
00:53:31,350 --> 00:53:33,080
Can we talk? Just one second.

750
00:53:34,490 --> 00:53:35,980
Please, Jack. Please.

751
00:53:36,050 --> 00:53:38,650
They'll put me on the street. They'll chop me.

752
00:53:40,860 --> 00:53:43,260
Here. Now just take...

753
00:53:44,030 --> 00:53:45,500
-Take this. -No, no...

754
00:53:45,560 --> 00:53:47,800
Just take the money. Please, just take the money.

755
00:53:47,870 --> 00:53:50,470
You must go. You must. Please, they are waiting.

756
00:53:50,540 --> 00:53:52,240
-Paul! -They are waiting.

757
00:53:52,310 --> 00:53:53,290
Paul.

758
00:53:54,650 --> 00:53:57,810
He won't put you out. Here, give her anything she wants.

759
00:53:57,880 --> 00:53:59,870
-Anything. Just charge it. -This is not necessary.

760
00:53:59,940 --> 00:54:02,280
-They're gonna kill us here. -Let him go.

761
00:54:02,350 --> 00:54:04,280
We have to let him go.

762
00:54:12,060 --> 00:54:14,460
Don't do that, please.

763
00:54:14,530 --> 00:54:16,520
Jesus Christ, I'm so ashamed.

764
00:54:28,710 --> 00:54:30,700
Wait! Wait!

765
00:54:35,420 --> 00:54:37,250
Hold the buses!

766
00:54:37,310 --> 00:54:38,510
Peter!

767
00:54:51,570 --> 00:54:54,890
Thank you for being here. Thank you very much. Thank you.

768
00:54:54,970 --> 00:54:57,030
-No Rwandans. -What?

769
00:54:57,100 --> 00:54:59,940
Foreign nationals only. Sorry, Father, those were the orders.

770
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:03,600
-But you can't leave the children behind. -Sorry, Father, we have our orders.

771
00:55:03,670 --> 00:55:05,160
-You can't leave them! -We can do no more.

772
00:55:05,250 --> 00:55:07,070
Father, it is of no use.

773
00:55:07,150 --> 00:55:10,480
These men are not here... They are not here to help us.

774
00:55:10,560 --> 00:55:12,210
Please, there is nothing we can do.

775
00:55:12,290 --> 00:55:14,440
Get your people on the bus. I will take care of the others.

776
00:55:14,520 --> 00:55:16,510
It is of no use, Father. Please, hurry.

777
00:55:20,460 --> 00:55:22,980
No, no, no. No, no, no. No.

778
00:55:23,070 --> 00:55:24,690
To the hotel. To the hotel.

779
00:55:28,910 --> 00:55:31,900
Sir, please, don't touch the camera. We have the right to film.

780
00:55:31,970 --> 00:55:34,600
-No filming. -Go to the hotel.

781
00:55:34,670 --> 00:55:36,140
Go inside.

782
00:55:37,250 --> 00:55:40,240
Go inside the hotel, all of you.

783
00:55:40,310 --> 00:55:42,650
Yes, you can stay, yes. We will take care of you.

784
00:55:42,710 --> 00:55:44,550
Go into the hotel.

785
00:55:48,960 --> 00:55:50,010
No!

786
00:55:51,050 --> 00:55:54,890
Go to the hotel. Go inside. Go inside the hotel.

787
00:56:43,880 --> 00:56:46,140
Excuse me. Excuse me.

788
00:56:50,420 --> 00:56:52,680
-Sir. -Come, Dube.

789
00:56:53,750 --> 00:56:56,820
-Please, everyone inside. -Please, people, let's go inside.

790
00:56:56,890 --> 00:56:59,860
Out of the rain, please. Come, sister, come.

791
00:57:05,630 --> 00:57:06,620
Paul.

792
00:57:10,940 --> 00:57:12,380
I want you to go.

793
00:57:13,850 --> 00:57:15,170
Go where?

794
00:57:17,780 --> 00:57:21,980
You take the children. You go get the girls.

795
00:57:22,050 --> 00:57:24,210
-Your card says Hutu... -What are you saying?

796
00:57:24,280 --> 00:57:27,680
Please, please. You pay money at the roadblocks.

797
00:57:27,760 --> 00:57:29,680
I want you to go.

798
00:57:29,760 --> 00:57:31,420
No, Tatiana, no.

799
00:57:32,730 --> 00:57:34,460
I will never leave you.

800
00:57:37,460 --> 00:57:39,120
I will never leave you.

801
00:57:44,940 --> 00:57:46,100
Oh, Tatsi.

802
00:57:50,440 --> 00:57:53,280
Let us sleep, my wife. Let us sleep.

803
00:58:06,560 --> 00:58:08,390
Get up. Get up.

804
00:58:08,460 --> 00:58:10,220
Get up, get up, get up.

805
00:58:12,200 --> 00:58:15,870
-Are you the manager? -Yes, sir. What's the matter?

806
00:58:17,770 --> 00:58:19,570
Everyone must leave the hotel now.

807
00:58:19,640 --> 00:58:21,830
-Why? -Papa, what's wrong?

808
00:58:21,910 --> 00:58:23,210
It's an order.

809
00:58:24,710 --> 00:58:28,700
I need some time... 20, 30 minutes... to take a shower.

810
00:58:30,120 --> 00:58:33,380
-Sir, people are still sleeping. -I don't care.

811
00:58:35,320 --> 00:58:39,450
Please, let me get you some beers. You and your boys.

812
00:58:39,520 --> 00:58:42,590
And I'll be down right away, all right? As quick as I can.

813
00:58:42,660 --> 00:58:45,660
-Ten minutes. -Yes, sir, ten minutes.

814
00:58:47,800 --> 00:58:49,930
-Get out of the way. -Quick, children, quickly.

815
00:58:50,000 --> 00:58:53,030
-Roger's not here. -Where is he? Where's Roger?

816
00:58:53,110 --> 00:58:54,270
Under the bed.

817
00:58:55,780 --> 00:58:58,110
Roger. It's Papa.

818
00:58:58,180 --> 00:59:00,080
They've gone. They've gone, they've gone.

819
00:59:00,150 --> 00:59:02,440
Come, come. Come on.

820
00:59:06,350 --> 00:59:09,010
Oh, my darling. It's okay, sweetie. It's okay.

821
00:59:09,090 --> 00:59:11,360
Come on, it's okay. It's okay.

822
00:59:11,420 --> 00:59:13,940
-Go to the roof, Tatiana. -The roof?

823
00:59:14,030 --> 00:59:16,220
Yes, yes, go to the roof right now.

824
00:59:17,000 --> 00:59:19,600
Yes, good day. General Bizimungu, please.

825
00:59:20,810 --> 00:59:22,570
He is where?

826
00:59:22,640 --> 00:59:24,700
No, that is unacceptable.

827
00:59:24,770 --> 00:59:26,440
Who would order such a thing?

828
00:59:28,510 --> 00:59:30,840
Yes, did you find the general?

829
00:59:34,410 --> 00:59:36,750
Gentlemen, please have some beer.

830
00:59:36,820 --> 00:59:38,410
Get me the guest list.

831
00:59:39,690 --> 00:59:40,850
Yes, sir.

832
00:59:43,620 --> 00:59:44,610
Yes?

833
00:59:44,690 --> 00:59:48,630
Sorry, sir, but I have a call from Paul in Kigali. He says it's urgent.

834
00:59:48,700 --> 00:59:50,630
Paul, are you all right?

835
00:59:50,700 --> 00:59:52,220
We have a big problem, sir.

836
00:59:52,300 --> 00:59:53,390
What?

837
00:59:53,460 --> 00:59:55,590
The Hutu army have come.

838
00:59:55,670 --> 00:59:58,230
They've ordered us... all of us... out of the hotel.

839
00:59:58,300 --> 01:00:00,060
Why are they doing this?

840
01:00:00,140 --> 01:00:02,610
I think they will kill us all.

841
01:00:02,680 --> 01:00:03,660
Kill?

842
01:00:05,310 --> 01:00:08,980
What do you mean... all? How many?

843
01:00:09,050 --> 01:00:13,920
We have 100 staff and now more than 800 guests.

844
01:00:13,980 --> 01:00:15,980
-800?! -Yes, sir.

845
01:00:16,060 --> 01:00:19,250
There are now 800 Tutsi and Hutu refugees.

846
01:00:19,320 --> 01:00:21,890
I do not have much time left, sir.

847
01:00:25,660 --> 01:00:27,530
I want to thank you

848
01:00:27,600 --> 01:00:29,900
for everything that you have done for me and my family,

849
01:00:29,970 --> 01:00:33,100
and please thank all of my friends at Sabena.

850
01:00:34,610 --> 01:00:36,160
Paul, wait.

851
01:00:36,750 --> 01:00:39,510
I'm gonna put you on hold. Stay by the phone.

852
01:00:40,650 --> 01:00:43,450
-Where are your papers? -We don't have any papers, sir.

853
01:00:43,510 --> 01:00:46,820
We don't have any papers. They got burnt in the house.

854
01:00:47,730 --> 01:00:50,380
Louis, get on to the U.N. Tell them what's happening.

855
01:00:50,460 --> 01:00:51,890
Did you need something, sir?

856
01:00:51,960 --> 01:00:56,360
Mary, call the prime minister's office. Tell them I must speak with him now.

857
01:00:56,430 --> 01:00:57,560
Okay.

858
01:01:01,100 --> 01:01:02,660
Paul, are you there?

859
01:01:03,500 --> 01:01:04,490
Yes, sir.

860
01:01:04,580 --> 01:01:06,300
Who can I call to stop this?

861
01:01:08,840 --> 01:01:11,910
The French. They supply the Hutu army.

862
01:01:13,210 --> 01:01:17,050
Do everything you can to buy time. I'll call you right back.

863
01:01:21,020 --> 01:01:23,540
What are you doing, Dube?

864
01:01:23,630 --> 01:01:26,560
The lieutenant, sir, he wants to see the guest list.

865
01:01:29,660 --> 01:01:32,820
-Go and get these boys some more beer. -Thirsty, boy? You like beer?

866
01:01:32,900 --> 01:01:34,230
Thank you.

867
01:01:37,140 --> 01:01:38,460
Come with me, please.

868
01:01:43,110 --> 01:01:45,270
Sir, that was two weeks ago.

869
01:01:50,550 --> 01:01:52,040
Here you are, sir.

870
01:01:54,960 --> 01:01:57,320
Anderson, Arthurs, Boulier...

871
01:01:58,690 --> 01:02:00,180
What is this?

872
01:02:03,130 --> 01:02:04,620
It is the guest list, sir.

873
01:02:05,640 --> 01:02:07,720
Are you trying to make a fool of me?

874
01:02:07,810 --> 01:02:12,890
No. We stopped taking names after the president was murdered.

875
01:02:12,980 --> 01:02:16,460
-This is the only guest list, sir. -There are no Europeans left!

876
01:02:17,580 --> 01:02:21,910
Get me the names of all the cockroaches in there now.

877
01:02:22,820 --> 01:02:25,750
-That will take time. -We don't have time.

878
01:02:25,820 --> 01:02:30,520
If I don't have the names so that I can pick out the traitors,

879
01:02:30,590 --> 01:02:33,430
then I'll kill everyone in there.

880
01:02:34,930 --> 01:02:36,420
Starting with you.

881
01:02:37,200 --> 01:02:38,720
Leave.

882
01:02:41,130 --> 01:02:42,190
Yes, sir.

883
01:02:54,450 --> 01:02:55,840
Yes, sir.

884
01:02:56,520 --> 01:02:57,680
Who did you call?

885
01:02:58,860 --> 01:03:01,180
-Who did I call? -Don't lie to me!

886
01:03:03,590 --> 01:03:05,580
What is your name?

887
01:03:05,660 --> 01:03:07,990
Rusesabagina.

888
01:03:09,100 --> 01:03:11,030
Paul Rusesabagina.

889
01:03:11,540 --> 01:03:13,390
I'll remember you.

890
01:03:14,660 --> 01:03:16,060
I'll remember you.

891
01:03:17,040 --> 01:03:20,760
-Let's go. -Come on, we're leaving.

892
01:03:30,320 --> 01:03:31,310
They've gone.

893
01:03:34,650 --> 01:03:36,050
Paul. Paul.

894
01:03:38,730 --> 01:03:40,720
I was afraid for you.

895
01:03:42,070 --> 01:03:45,730
Sir, the president of Sabena is on the phone for you.

896
01:03:47,100 --> 01:03:49,030
I must talk with this man.

897
01:03:54,870 --> 01:03:57,600
-Mr. Tillens. -Paul, what's going on?

898
01:03:57,680 --> 01:04:01,010
They left. Thank you, sir. What did you do?

899
01:04:01,090 --> 01:04:04,170
I got through to the French president's office.

900
01:04:06,420 --> 01:04:08,750
Well, thank you. You have saved our lives.

901
01:04:09,590 --> 01:04:14,220
I pleaded with the French and the Belgians to go back and get you all.

902
01:04:15,160 --> 01:04:17,790
I am afraid this is not going to happen.

903
01:04:19,470 --> 01:04:21,960
They're cowards, Paul.

904
01:04:22,870 --> 01:04:26,600
Rwanda is not worth a single vote to any of them.

905
01:04:28,010 --> 01:04:30,940
The French, the British, the Americans.

906
01:04:32,040 --> 01:04:33,700
I am sorry, Paul.

907
01:04:35,990 --> 01:04:37,070
Thank you.

908
01:04:40,720 --> 01:04:42,350
There will be no rescue...

909
01:04:43,800 --> 01:04:45,790
...no intervention for us.

910
01:04:47,330 --> 01:04:49,660
We can only save ourselves.

911
01:04:50,870 --> 01:04:53,020
Many of you know influential people abroad.

912
01:04:53,100 --> 01:04:54,590
You must call these people.

913
01:04:54,670 --> 01:04:57,690
Please, fax this to this number. Thank you.

914
01:04:57,770 --> 01:05:00,500
You must tell them what will happen to us.

915
01:05:02,180 --> 01:05:03,670
Say good-bye.

916
01:05:06,610 --> 01:05:08,370
But when you say good-bye,

917
01:05:08,450 --> 01:05:13,620
say it as though you are reaching through the phone and holding their hand.

918
01:05:14,520 --> 01:05:17,210
Let them know that if they let go of that hand...

919
01:05:19,330 --> 01:05:20,810
...you will die.

920
01:05:24,170 --> 01:05:27,890
We must shame them into sending help.

921
01:05:30,340 --> 01:05:35,290
Most importantly, this cannot be a refugee camp.

922
01:05:35,380 --> 01:05:39,480
The Interhamwe believe that the Mille Collines is a four-star Sabena hotel.

923
01:05:39,550 --> 01:05:43,240
That is the only thing that is keeping us alive.

924
01:05:43,310 --> 01:05:45,250
Have you printed the bills?

925
01:05:46,750 --> 01:05:49,250
Thank you. Now please erase the register.

926
01:05:49,320 --> 01:05:52,350
-Erase it? -Yes. I want no names to appear there.

927
01:05:53,060 --> 01:05:55,020
Boss, the carpenters are ready.

928
01:05:55,100 --> 01:05:57,830
Tell them to remove all of the numbers from the doors.

929
01:05:57,900 --> 01:05:59,920
-And put what? -And put nothing.

930
01:06:07,780 --> 01:06:10,430
Good day. Here is your bill for the last week.

931
01:06:10,510 --> 01:06:13,180
If you cannot pay or think you will not be able to pay,

932
01:06:13,250 --> 01:06:16,650
please go to the banquet room and Dube will take care of you. Thank you.

933
01:06:20,790 --> 01:06:23,260
Does the State Department have a view

934
01:06:23,320 --> 01:06:27,520
as to whether or not what is happening could be genocide?

935
01:06:27,600 --> 01:06:31,000
We have every reason to believe that acts of genocide have occurred.

936
01:06:31,060 --> 01:06:35,790
How many acts of genocide does it take to make genocide?

937
01:06:35,870 --> 01:06:38,900
Alan, that's just not a question that I'm in a position to answer.

938
01:06:38,970 --> 01:06:42,530
Is it true that you have specific guidance

939
01:06:42,610 --> 01:06:45,100
not to use the word "genocide" in isolation,

940
01:06:45,180 --> 01:06:47,770
but always to preface it with this word "acts of"?

941
01:06:49,320 --> 01:06:54,370
I have guidance which I try to use as best as I can.

942
01:06:54,460 --> 01:06:56,010
I have...

943
01:06:56,080 --> 01:06:58,520
There are formulations that we are using

944
01:06:58,600 --> 01:07:01,580
that we are trying to be consistent in our use of...

945
01:07:04,200 --> 01:07:06,000
I'm sorry it is not Glenmorangie.

946
01:07:07,100 --> 01:07:08,760
As long as it is scotch.

947
01:07:11,070 --> 01:07:14,800
Your white friends have abandoned you.

948
01:07:16,540 --> 01:07:19,200
-So it would seem. -Well, don't worry.

949
01:07:19,270 --> 01:07:22,580
-I will take care of you. -I'm glad to hear that

950
01:07:22,650 --> 01:07:25,580
because I was wondering if perhaps you could spare us a few policemen.

951
01:07:25,660 --> 01:07:26,840
To protect us, sir.

952
01:07:26,920 --> 01:07:29,910
-The police are very busy, Paul. -Yes, I'm aware of this.

953
01:07:29,990 --> 01:07:33,260
But when I last spoke to the president of Sabena,

954
01:07:33,330 --> 01:07:36,730
he assured me that anyone who helped protect Belgian property

955
01:07:36,800 --> 01:07:38,280
would be well rewarded.

956
01:07:39,290 --> 01:07:40,630
I will see what I can do.

957
01:07:41,810 --> 01:07:43,460
Excuse me momentarily, sir.

958
01:07:45,210 --> 01:07:46,970
Where has all our beer gone?

959
01:07:47,980 --> 01:07:50,700
Sir, Gregoire has been taking beer.

960
01:07:51,410 --> 01:07:52,810
How much beer?

961
01:07:53,750 --> 01:07:54,840
Many.

962
01:07:58,220 --> 01:08:01,150
...come down to the reception. And then he says to me,

963
01:08:01,220 --> 01:08:02,850
"How do you want the girls?"

964
01:08:04,830 --> 01:08:07,760
There's our cockroach manager. Always kissing ass.

965
01:08:13,460 --> 01:08:14,630
General...

966
01:08:16,370 --> 01:08:18,100
I'm glad you came by.

967
01:08:18,880 --> 01:08:21,340
I overheard something that I think you should know about.

968
01:08:21,410 --> 01:08:22,640
What did you overhear?

969
01:08:22,710 --> 01:08:26,980
It was a discussion between a U.N. Colonel and an American Embassy official.

970
01:08:27,050 --> 01:08:28,450
And what did they say?

971
01:08:28,520 --> 01:08:31,350
The American assured the colonel that they would watch everything.

972
01:08:31,420 --> 01:08:32,970
How? They have gone, Paul.

973
01:08:33,060 --> 01:08:36,140
With their spies. Satellites.

974
01:08:38,660 --> 01:08:40,490
Americans.

975
01:08:40,560 --> 01:08:42,460
Oh, Gregoire!

976
01:08:46,270 --> 01:08:48,160
You know, I admire you, General.

977
01:08:48,870 --> 01:08:51,670
How do you keep command of your men amid such madness?

978
01:08:51,740 --> 01:08:55,510
-I am a strong man, Paul. -I wish I were more like you.

979
01:08:56,440 --> 01:08:58,810
-I mean, look at my staff. -Cheers.

980
01:08:58,880 --> 01:09:01,540
He won't work, listens to no one.

981
01:09:01,620 --> 01:09:04,210
-He is staff? -Oh, yes.

982
01:09:04,290 --> 01:09:05,280
Yes.

983
01:09:16,030 --> 01:09:18,190
Get back to work, you slug! Go!

984
01:09:19,560 --> 01:09:21,000
Satellites?

985
01:09:22,170 --> 01:09:25,660
What was I going to say, that the Americans were hiding in the trees?

986
01:09:37,710 --> 01:09:41,520
-What's the matter? -I have to go out and get food.

987
01:09:41,580 --> 01:09:45,520
-Go out? Where? -To George Rutaganda's place.

988
01:09:45,590 --> 01:09:47,710
No. No, no.

989
01:09:47,800 --> 01:09:49,620
I have to, Tatiana.

990
01:09:49,700 --> 01:09:52,320
We are only as valuable as the money we give to him.

991
01:09:52,400 --> 01:09:54,060
You cannot go alone.

992
01:09:54,940 --> 01:09:58,600
I'm not going alone. I'll take Gregoire with me.

993
01:09:58,670 --> 01:10:01,910
He's a good Hutu, and he wants to impress me now.

994
01:10:11,750 --> 01:10:13,920
It is good to see you back at work, Gregoire.

995
01:10:13,990 --> 01:10:17,050
-Please, sir, accept my humblest apologies. -Please, please.

996
01:10:17,920 --> 01:10:19,760
We have a job this morning.

997
01:10:19,830 --> 01:10:22,150
We are going to see George Rutaganda.

998
01:10:23,230 --> 01:10:24,560
Please get the van.

999
01:10:44,310 --> 01:10:45,800
Show me your I.D.

1000
01:10:45,890 --> 01:10:48,380
Remember how those Tutsi women used to look down

1001
01:10:48,450 --> 01:10:50,080
their long noses at Hutu men?

1002
01:10:50,080 --> 01:10:51,490
Now they beg for their lives.

1003
01:10:51,560 --> 01:10:54,080
I'm here to see my friend George Rutaganda.

1004
01:10:54,170 --> 01:10:58,530
I say taste those Tutsi whores before they die.

1005
01:10:58,600 --> 01:11:02,120
Then they'll know what Hutu power is, my warriors.

1006
01:11:02,210 --> 01:11:05,970
Remember, one cockroach can start an infestation.

1007
01:11:06,040 --> 01:11:08,500
We need to exterminate these vermin.

1008
01:11:39,240 --> 01:11:41,610
Hey, Paul, my old friend.

1009
01:11:45,050 --> 01:11:49,000
Tutsi prostitutes and witches. So, what can I do for you?

1010
01:11:49,750 --> 01:11:52,350
-I need supplies, George. -Anytime.

1011
01:11:57,430 --> 01:12:01,010
Paul, everything is double the price now. You understand that?

1012
01:12:01,100 --> 01:12:04,260
Yes. I need rice, beans,

1013
01:12:04,330 --> 01:12:07,730
powdered milk, beer, and your best whiskey.

1014
01:12:08,900 --> 01:12:12,390
Beer yes, but whiskey no.

1015
01:12:12,470 --> 01:12:14,030
You have no whiskey?

1016
01:12:14,110 --> 01:12:16,800
No whiskey, no spirits.

1017
01:12:16,870 --> 01:12:21,610
Your... rich guests will have to do without their scotch.

1018
01:12:22,210 --> 01:12:25,710
Anyway, Paul, I have bled that cow enough now.

1019
01:12:26,820 --> 01:12:28,340
What are you saying, George?

1020
01:12:28,420 --> 01:12:34,020
Your rich cockroaches at the hotel, their money is no good to them anymore.

1021
01:12:34,860 --> 01:12:37,090
Soon all the Tutsis will be dead.

1022
01:12:39,670 --> 01:12:42,930
You do not honestly believe that you can kill them all?

1023
01:12:44,310 --> 01:12:45,700
And why not?

1024
01:12:47,340 --> 01:12:48,940
Why not?

1025
01:12:49,010 --> 01:12:51,500
We are halfway there already.

1026
01:12:54,320 --> 01:12:57,180
So, Paul, you want 12 bags of rice?

1027
01:12:58,380 --> 01:13:00,980
Give him 12 bags of rice and 4 crates of beer.

1028
01:13:01,050 --> 01:13:02,540
Yes, sir, right away.

1029
01:13:04,090 --> 01:13:09,900
Oh, and, Paul, I'll give you a crate of soft drinks for the kids free of charge.

1030
01:13:11,400 --> 01:13:12,490
Yes.

1031
01:13:14,230 --> 01:13:16,960
Ten bags of beans. Come, quick.

1032
01:13:17,600 --> 01:13:20,120
And put those in the van. You.

1033
01:13:21,740 --> 01:13:23,730
Let me give you a little tip, my friend.

1034
01:13:23,810 --> 01:13:26,540
Our generals in army say, "Don't go near the Mille Collines

1035
01:13:26,610 --> 01:13:28,810
or they will send the Belgian soldiers back here.

1036
01:13:28,880 --> 01:13:33,150
But soon those generals will have gone and we will be in charge.

1037
01:13:34,390 --> 01:13:38,620
It's time to butcher that fat cow of yours for the meat.

1038
01:13:49,540 --> 01:13:50,940
Let's go.

1039
01:13:53,880 --> 01:13:55,870
Maybe you could help us, Paul.

1040
01:13:55,940 --> 01:13:58,810
You have some very important traitors at that hotel.

1041
01:13:59,480 --> 01:14:01,310
Now, if we were to get them,

1042
01:14:01,380 --> 01:14:05,180
then maybe we would let you have one or two cockroaches of your own.

1043
01:14:07,120 --> 01:14:08,520
Do you understand?

1044
01:14:10,560 --> 01:14:13,390
It is almost dawn, George.

1045
01:14:13,460 --> 01:14:15,550
We really must be going.

1046
01:14:17,330 --> 01:14:20,530
Take the river road back. It's clear.

1047
01:14:42,220 --> 01:14:44,810
-Gregoire. -What is going on now?

1048
01:14:44,890 --> 01:14:47,120
-You've driven off the road. -No, I'm on the road.

1049
01:14:47,190 --> 01:14:50,030
You're going to put us in the river. Stop the car, stop the car.

1050
01:16:14,580 --> 01:16:16,280
Back up the car, Gregoire.

1051
01:16:18,190 --> 01:16:19,350
Listen to me.

1052
01:16:20,950 --> 01:16:24,120
You will tell no one what you have seen here today.

1053
01:16:24,190 --> 01:16:25,590
No one, Gregoire.

1054
01:16:41,910 --> 01:16:45,900
Dube. Please help Gregoire to unload the van. Thank you.

1055
01:17:20,250 --> 01:17:21,650
Oh, dear.

1056
01:17:53,780 --> 01:17:55,050
Oh, God!

1057
01:17:58,250 --> 01:17:59,480
Oh, God!

1058
01:18:00,690 --> 01:18:02,020
-Sir. -Dube!

1059
01:18:02,080 --> 01:18:05,950
-Sir, are you okay? -Don't come in. Don't come in.

1060
01:18:06,020 --> 01:18:08,020
I'll be out in a minute.

1061
01:18:09,300 --> 01:18:12,120
-Sir, are you okay? -Yes, I'm all right, Dube.

1062
01:18:13,030 --> 01:18:14,830
Don't come in. I'll be out.

1063
01:18:49,130 --> 01:18:50,390
Hundreds.

1064
01:18:53,130 --> 01:18:55,230
It was too many to count.

1065
01:18:58,780 --> 01:19:01,250
Why are people so cruel?

1066
01:19:05,220 --> 01:19:06,380
Hatred.

1067
01:19:07,860 --> 01:19:09,680
Insanity. I don't know.

1068
01:19:15,400 --> 01:19:16,420
There you go.

1069
01:19:16,490 --> 01:19:18,800
Is she putting her fingers in the soup?

1070
01:19:18,870 --> 01:19:20,770
Oh, yes.

1071
01:19:21,930 --> 01:19:24,430
...to do with you. Nothing to do with me.

1072
01:19:24,500 --> 01:19:25,910
I remember...

1073
01:19:27,000 --> 01:19:28,730
No, no, no, you make a mistake.

1074
01:19:28,810 --> 01:19:30,510
-Hello. -Come with me.

1075
01:19:32,510 --> 01:19:34,450
-Where are we going? -Just come.

1076
01:19:51,300 --> 01:19:52,630
It's beautiful.

1077
01:19:54,630 --> 01:19:55,900
You like it?

1078
01:20:05,370 --> 01:20:07,780
I hear we must pay for everything.

1079
01:20:07,840 --> 01:20:09,340
Yes, this is true.

1080
01:20:10,650 --> 01:20:14,140
So... how much for this?

1081
01:20:16,150 --> 01:20:17,650
A kiss.

1082
01:20:29,500 --> 01:20:34,340
You are a good man, Paul Rusesabagina.

1083
01:20:51,020 --> 01:20:52,620
I have a confession.

1084
01:20:54,690 --> 01:20:56,690
When you worked as the nurse...

1085
01:20:56,760 --> 01:20:58,930
-In Ruhengeri? -Yes.

1086
01:20:59,000 --> 01:21:01,020
When we first met...

1087
01:21:02,600 --> 01:21:05,090
I had you transferred to Kigali.

1088
01:21:07,440 --> 01:21:08,770
What?

1089
01:21:09,740 --> 01:21:14,230
I bribed the Minister of Health to have you transferred to Kigali.

1090
01:21:16,110 --> 01:21:18,710
-Why? -To be closer.

1091
01:21:20,190 --> 01:21:21,920
So that I could marry you.

1092
01:21:28,590 --> 01:21:29,930
What was the bribe?

1093
01:21:32,730 --> 01:21:35,890
-What am I worth to you? -It was substantial.

1094
01:21:35,960 --> 01:21:38,800
-Tell me what it was. -A car.

1095
01:21:40,910 --> 01:21:43,740
-What sort of car? -What does that matter?

1096
01:21:43,810 --> 01:21:45,670
I want to know.

1097
01:21:47,250 --> 01:21:48,840
A Volkswagen.

1098
01:21:53,860 --> 01:21:55,180
I hope it was a new one.

1099
01:22:20,280 --> 01:22:23,440
We have had a good life, you and I. Yes.

1100
01:22:26,420 --> 01:22:31,020
I thank God every day for the time we've had.

1101
01:22:37,070 --> 01:22:40,970
-We have to have a plan. -A plan?

1102
01:22:42,830 --> 01:22:45,830
Our children cannot see us die first.

1103
01:22:45,910 --> 01:22:49,310
If the militia come, you must come up here as quick as you can.

1104
01:22:49,370 --> 01:22:52,040
-Please, I don't want to... -You must come up here, Tatiana.

1105
01:22:52,110 --> 01:22:55,040
-I don't want you to talk like this, please. -We have to, Tatiana.

1106
01:22:56,850 --> 01:22:59,250
If I do not make it,

1107
01:22:59,320 --> 01:23:02,110
you must take all of our children by the hand...

1108
01:23:03,890 --> 01:23:05,220
...and you must jump.

1109
01:23:07,290 --> 01:23:10,620
-What are you saying? I could never... -You have to, Tatiana.

1110
01:23:10,690 --> 01:23:13,460
-You have to promise me. -What are you saying?

1111
01:23:13,530 --> 01:23:16,840
Tatiana, the machete is no way to die. You have to promise me you will do it.

1112
01:23:16,900 --> 01:23:18,630
I cannot do...

1113
01:23:18,700 --> 01:23:21,470
You have to promise me, Tatiana. Please.

1114
01:23:21,540 --> 01:23:23,130
Promise me you will do it.

1115
01:23:26,780 --> 01:23:28,610
Please, Tatiana.

1116
01:23:31,750 --> 01:23:32,910
Yes.

1117
01:23:35,750 --> 01:23:37,480
I'm sorry. I love you.

1118
01:23:39,220 --> 01:23:40,560
I love you.

1119
01:23:48,430 --> 01:23:49,920
I'm gonna get you!

1120
01:23:51,370 --> 01:23:53,360
Diane, Elys, you know better.

1121
01:23:53,430 --> 01:23:55,970
No one can be at the front of the hotel. I have told you this.

1122
01:23:56,040 --> 01:23:58,340
-Take these children in the back. Hurry. -Sorry, Papa.

1123
01:23:59,540 --> 01:24:01,380
-Come, children. Come. -Thank you, Dube.

1124
01:24:04,110 --> 01:24:07,340
Paul, I've got good news.

1125
01:24:10,360 --> 01:24:14,090
Congratulations. Your calls have worked.

1126
01:24:14,160 --> 01:24:17,960
I have exit visas for the following families.

1127
01:24:18,030 --> 01:24:21,220
Abukesu, Tanzania.

1128
01:24:21,300 --> 01:24:24,290
Bidori, Kenya.

1129
01:24:26,210 --> 01:24:28,300
Gituaranga, Zambia.

1130
01:24:28,380 --> 01:24:30,140
Hallelujah!

1131
01:24:30,210 --> 01:24:31,870
Khalesa, Belgium.

1132
01:24:31,940 --> 01:24:33,100
Oh, thank you!

1133
01:24:34,280 --> 01:24:35,670
Dakuzi...

1134
01:24:37,250 --> 01:24:38,510
Kenya.

1135
01:24:39,390 --> 01:24:42,150
Masambo, Zambia.

1136
01:24:43,390 --> 01:24:45,720
Zinguru, Ghana.

1137
01:24:45,790 --> 01:24:48,850
Rusesabagina, Belgium.

1138
01:24:50,130 --> 01:24:51,600
All right, that's it.

1139
01:24:53,070 --> 01:24:56,060
So remember, families be ready at 7 a. m.

1140
01:24:56,130 --> 01:24:57,390
Let's go.

1141
01:24:57,470 --> 01:24:58,530
-Colonel? -Yeah.

1142
01:24:59,610 --> 01:25:01,810
Now, certainly Odette and Jean Baptiste are on the list.

1143
01:25:01,880 --> 01:25:04,700
I'm sorry, Jean, Odette.

1144
01:25:05,880 --> 01:25:09,440
But I have been assured there will be another plane soon.

1145
01:25:09,510 --> 01:25:10,500
Excuse me.

1146
01:25:13,010 --> 01:25:16,080
Don't worry, Tatsi, we'll make it to the next list.

1147
01:25:16,150 --> 01:25:17,140
Yeah.

1148
01:25:18,760 --> 01:25:21,690
The girls... Paul, I will not leave without them.

1149
01:25:31,700 --> 01:25:33,030
What have you brought us?

1150
01:25:33,110 --> 01:25:36,430
Antibiotics, medical supplies, general first aid.

1151
01:25:36,510 --> 01:25:38,000
Thank you.

1152
01:25:38,080 --> 01:25:40,570
-I hear there's to be a convoy. -Yes.

1153
01:25:40,650 --> 01:25:42,380
Are you on the list?

1154
01:25:45,850 --> 01:25:50,580
Madame Archer, I have an impossible request of you.

1155
01:25:51,550 --> 01:25:54,830
Is there any way that you could return to the old woman

1156
01:25:54,890 --> 01:25:56,880
and bring the girls back here to us?

1157
01:25:56,960 --> 01:26:00,930
Paul, that side of town has been destroyed in the fighting.

1158
01:26:01,870 --> 01:26:03,200
They're probably dead.

1159
01:26:06,280 --> 01:26:09,600
Madame Archer, I'm begging you. Those girls have no one now.

1160
01:26:13,380 --> 01:26:14,870
I'll try.

1161
01:26:16,010 --> 01:26:18,110
We have to leave by 7 a. m.

1162
01:26:18,620 --> 01:26:20,710
Who'll take care of the orphans when you're gone?

1163
01:26:20,790 --> 01:26:24,450
Odette. Odette will care for them until we can get them out of here.

1164
01:26:28,660 --> 01:26:32,660
Tell me, Paul, what country's gonna take 20 Rwandan orphans?

1165
01:26:32,730 --> 01:26:36,460
I will find someone. I promise you.

1166
01:26:38,700 --> 01:26:40,830
-Thanks. -Thank you.

1167
01:26:48,350 --> 01:26:49,750
Come on, take my hand.

1168
01:26:50,350 --> 01:26:53,680
News Service Africa. Today a Red Cross representative

1169
01:26:53,750 --> 01:26:56,320
claimed that the death rate in the Rwandan conflict

1170
01:26:56,390 --> 01:26:59,950
may have climbed to as many as 500,000 victims.

1171
01:27:00,030 --> 01:27:02,430
One report stated that 40,000 bodies

1172
01:27:02,500 --> 01:27:04,730
had been removed from Lake Victoria.

1173
01:27:06,600 --> 01:27:07,620
Where is she?

1174
01:27:07,700 --> 01:27:11,470
I don't know. We wait until seven.

1175
01:27:11,540 --> 01:27:13,940
If she is not back with the girls by then...

1176
01:27:15,300 --> 01:27:16,790
...she may not be coming.

1177
01:27:19,610 --> 01:27:20,600
Thank you.

1178
01:27:20,680 --> 01:27:22,920
Please, take these letters.

1179
01:27:22,980 --> 01:27:25,250
Yes, I will take your letters.

1180
01:27:25,310 --> 01:27:27,780
Thank you so much, Paul, taking the letter.

1181
01:27:29,320 --> 01:27:32,150
-Thank you so much. -Yes, I am sorry.

1182
01:27:32,230 --> 01:27:33,380
Thank you very much.

1183
01:27:33,460 --> 01:27:36,220
I am sorry. I wish I could have done more. I am sorry.

1184
01:27:38,530 --> 01:27:40,360
God be with you.

1185
01:27:41,770 --> 01:27:44,930
-Yes, do you have any children? -Yes, you're clear to go.

1186
01:27:46,270 --> 01:27:48,110
No, sorry, no good.

1187
01:27:48,610 --> 01:27:50,970
Come. Come, children.

1188
01:27:51,050 --> 01:27:52,770
Tatsi, come.

1189
01:27:54,640 --> 01:27:56,980
Please, Paul, the girls. We wait a little longer.

1190
01:27:57,050 --> 01:27:59,040
We cannot wait. We cannot wait, Tatsi.

1191
01:27:59,120 --> 01:28:00,110
There you go.

1192
01:28:00,750 --> 01:28:02,080
Let's move out!

1193
01:28:05,790 --> 01:28:07,130
Good luck, sir.

1194
01:28:18,530 --> 01:28:23,130
I am not leaving. You hold Tatiana. Take care of my family.

1195
01:28:29,310 --> 01:28:30,810
Paul. Paul!

1196
01:28:31,980 --> 01:28:35,480
I cannot leave these people to die. I cannot leave these people.

1197
01:28:35,550 --> 01:28:36,810
Papa!

1198
01:28:36,880 --> 01:28:39,860
Roger! Roger, I will follow on the next flight.

1199
01:28:39,930 --> 01:28:42,690
No, don't leave me! Paul!

1200
01:28:42,770 --> 01:28:46,220
Don't worry. Don't worry, children. Your father's going to be okay.

1201
01:28:46,300 --> 01:28:47,320
Papa!

1202
01:28:47,400 --> 01:28:51,170
-Don't worry. He's okay. -I want Papa!

1203
01:28:51,230 --> 01:28:52,700
It's okay.

1204
01:29:18,230 --> 01:29:21,560
I say those Hutus who shelter the cockroaches

1205
01:29:21,640 --> 01:29:23,960
are the same as cockroaches.

1206
01:29:26,100 --> 01:29:27,970
-They are all the same. -This is crazy.

1207
01:29:28,040 --> 01:29:32,100
Their fate should be the same. This is RTLM.

1208
01:29:43,160 --> 01:29:47,320
The Tutsi cockroaches of the rebel army must be denied recruits.

1209
01:29:47,390 --> 01:29:50,990
Come on, good Hutus. The graves are not yet full.

1210
01:29:51,060 --> 01:29:53,930
-Who will help us fill them? -That goddamn radio station.

1211
01:29:55,040 --> 01:29:58,300
Okay. Yeah, they are going to the airport.

1212
01:30:01,880 --> 01:30:05,900
Stand by your radios. I am hearing some urgent news.

1213
01:30:07,110 --> 01:30:10,210
-Boss! Please, come quick! -Not now, Dube.

1214
01:30:10,280 --> 01:30:13,250
It is important! It is on the radio. You have to hear it.

1215
01:30:14,620 --> 01:30:17,880
We have received reports of very important cockroaches

1216
01:30:17,950 --> 01:30:21,790
and traitors trying to escape from the Mille Collines Hotel.

1217
01:30:21,860 --> 01:30:23,390
Gather up your weapons.

1218
01:30:23,460 --> 01:30:26,630
Stand by your radios. We will keep you informed.

1219
01:30:26,700 --> 01:30:29,920
-They are being smuggled away... -No, no! Who told them of this, Dube?

1220
01:30:30,000 --> 01:30:31,990
I saw Gregoire, sir. It is Gregoire.

1221
01:30:31,990 --> 01:30:33,270
I saw him leaving in our bus.

1222
01:30:42,840 --> 01:30:45,340
Please, sir, I will give you whatever I have.

1223
01:30:45,420 --> 01:30:47,970
I say who leaves that hotel, and no one else.

1224
01:30:50,420 --> 01:30:53,320
General Bizimungu, they are driving into an ambush.

1225
01:31:13,750 --> 01:31:14,910
Slow down.

1226
01:31:16,780 --> 01:31:18,370
Stay calm.

1227
01:31:18,980 --> 01:31:20,880
-What is happening? -We're stopping.

1228
01:31:23,050 --> 01:31:25,280
You have got cockroaches in these trucks.

1229
01:31:25,360 --> 01:31:27,720
No, no. I've got U.N. Personnel in these trucks.

1230
01:31:27,800 --> 01:31:30,030
I've got permission to go through these roadblocks.

1231
01:31:30,100 --> 01:31:33,430
-I'm going to search these trucks. -You are not going to search this convoy.

1232
01:31:35,060 --> 01:31:37,190
-I am. -Cover me.

1233
01:31:44,240 --> 01:31:45,730
Go to the back.

1234
01:31:51,750 --> 01:31:55,370
Get away from that truck. Get away from that truck! Now!

1235
01:32:04,970 --> 01:32:07,100
Get back! You're not to hurt these people.

1236
01:32:08,670 --> 01:32:10,160
Get back! Move back!

1237
01:32:10,840 --> 01:32:13,240
Look, I told you, you've got cockroaches in your truck.

1238
01:32:13,310 --> 01:32:16,970
No, no, no. They're political refugees under U.N. Sanction.

1239
01:32:20,580 --> 01:32:24,750
News has come to us that we have cowards in our own army

1240
01:32:24,820 --> 01:32:26,980
who will not let us punish them.

1241
01:32:30,160 --> 01:32:31,140
No!

1242
01:32:33,260 --> 01:32:35,250
You're moving cockroaches from Mille Collines?

1243
01:32:35,330 --> 01:32:37,790
No, sir. No, sir, they're political refugees.

1244
01:32:37,870 --> 01:32:40,920
-They cannot leave Mille Collines. -They are not leaving.

1245
01:32:41,800 --> 01:32:42,830
Stop him!

1246
01:32:45,210 --> 01:32:46,570
You bastard!

1247
01:32:52,350 --> 01:32:53,400
What's your name?

1248
01:32:53,470 --> 01:32:55,840
-What's your name? -I can't think...

1249
01:32:56,640 --> 01:32:59,620
-Kill them! -Get everybody out of here! Move it!

1250
01:32:59,690 --> 01:33:02,520
What's your name? What's your name?

1251
01:33:03,120 --> 01:33:04,450
Let's move! Drive!

1252
01:33:04,530 --> 01:33:06,290
Move! Get out!

1253
01:33:06,360 --> 01:33:07,840
Out, or I'll shoot!

1254
01:33:11,100 --> 01:33:12,090
Get out!

1255
01:33:15,870 --> 01:33:17,460
Drive, drive! Let's go!

1256
01:33:18,410 --> 01:33:20,400
Help us get out of here.

1257
01:33:20,470 --> 01:33:22,230
Clear the street!

1258
01:33:31,890 --> 01:33:34,550
I am receiving more news, good Hutus.

1259
01:33:34,620 --> 01:33:38,460
I have learned that the traitor Rusesabagina's cockroaches

1260
01:33:38,520 --> 01:33:39,930
are on a truck.

1261
01:33:39,990 --> 01:33:42,220
10,000 francs for their heads!

1262
01:33:44,490 --> 01:33:47,150
Stay still. Give me your shirt, quickly.

1263
01:33:56,750 --> 01:33:58,740
Come on, Paul. Come on, come on!

1264
01:33:58,810 --> 01:34:01,830
Come on, here, here. Give me your hand. Come on.

1265
01:34:04,380 --> 01:34:05,680
Please, please.

1266
01:34:05,760 --> 01:34:08,580
-Hey, medic. Get a medic over here! -You need to hurry up, please.

1267
01:34:08,650 --> 01:34:10,380
Come, hurry, hurry.

1268
01:34:13,260 --> 01:34:15,690
-Let me help you. -Someone give this guard a hand, please.

1269
01:34:18,660 --> 01:34:20,160
Oh, Tatiana, my darling.

1270
01:34:23,230 --> 01:34:25,430
-I was so worried about you. -Move that truck out of the way!

1271
01:34:25,500 --> 01:34:26,490
Get him inside!

1272
01:34:27,310 --> 01:34:29,470
Tatiana. Tatiana.

1273
01:34:30,810 --> 01:34:33,300
You left me. You left me.

1274
01:34:33,380 --> 01:34:35,470
Take this. I don't want it. I don't want it.

1275
01:34:35,550 --> 01:34:38,340
You said you'd never leave me, and you left me. You are a liar!

1276
01:34:40,580 --> 01:34:42,710
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

1277
01:34:42,790 --> 01:34:44,590
-I'm sorry. -Papa, Papa.

1278
01:34:44,660 --> 01:34:47,560
-Papa, Mama! -I love you.

1279
01:34:56,200 --> 01:34:58,960
I wanted you to be safe, all of you.

1280
01:34:59,840 --> 01:35:02,500
That was not your decision to make.

1281
01:35:02,570 --> 01:35:06,010
We make our decisions together. That was our promise.

1282
01:35:06,080 --> 01:35:07,780
You're right.

1283
01:35:07,940 --> 01:35:09,880
You're right.

1284
01:35:09,940 --> 01:35:12,850
I knew that the minute the truck pulled away.

1285
01:35:12,920 --> 01:35:14,310
I'm sorry.

1286
01:35:14,660 --> 01:35:15,850
Come on, put some more water.

1287
01:35:15,920 --> 01:35:17,480
What are they doing?

1288
01:35:18,590 --> 01:35:20,110
Dube.

1289
01:35:20,890 --> 01:35:24,550
I'm sorry, sir. They shut down the water. This is all we have.

1290
01:35:31,100 --> 01:35:32,760
General.

1291
01:35:32,840 --> 01:35:34,300
Where are my supplies?

1292
01:35:35,140 --> 01:35:37,040
I'm sorry, sir. The cellar is empty.

1293
01:35:37,110 --> 01:35:42,170
You have nothing, and yet you call me, begging me for help?

1294
01:35:42,250 --> 01:35:44,580
Do you know the trouble I have protecting these cockroaches?

1295
01:35:44,650 --> 01:35:46,950
Sir, I have money from the guests.

1296
01:35:47,020 --> 01:35:48,950
Rwandan francs!

1297
01:35:49,920 --> 01:35:52,080
Those are only good for wiping your ass.

1298
01:35:53,650 --> 01:35:55,780
There is nothing more I can do for you, Paul.

1299
01:35:55,870 --> 01:35:58,520
No more police, no more protection.

1300
01:35:59,900 --> 01:36:02,770
Let the U.N. Take care of you.

1301
01:36:05,710 --> 01:36:07,430
Drive. Go!

1302
01:36:14,010 --> 01:36:16,140
What would Sabena make of this?

1303
01:36:23,960 --> 01:36:25,050
Watch out!

1304
01:36:31,030 --> 01:36:32,550
Get down, get down!

1305
01:36:37,100 --> 01:36:39,370
Are you hurt? Go outside.

1306
01:36:39,440 --> 01:36:41,960
Please stay still. There's glass here. I will get it out.

1307
01:36:42,040 --> 01:36:43,770
Is anyone hurt, Odette?

1308
01:36:43,840 --> 01:36:45,970
Lots of cuts and bruises.

1309
01:36:52,450 --> 01:36:54,320
Thank God it was a storeroom.

1310
01:36:56,260 --> 01:36:59,190
And in Rwanda, humanitarian agencies report

1311
01:36:59,260 --> 01:37:01,790
that a rapid advance by the Tutsi rebel army

1312
01:37:01,860 --> 01:37:05,730
has sparked a mass evacuation of Hutu refugees towards the Congo.

1313
01:37:05,800 --> 01:37:07,960
One aid worker described it

1314
01:37:08,030 --> 01:37:11,060
as the largest refugee exodus in modern history.

1315
01:37:11,140 --> 01:37:12,830
The rebels have taken half the city,

1316
01:37:12,900 --> 01:37:17,100
and they have proposed a deal the Hutu generals are willing to accept.

1317
01:37:18,010 --> 01:37:21,030
The rebels will exchange their Hutu prisoners,

1318
01:37:21,120 --> 01:37:22,940
and you people, all of you,

1319
01:37:23,020 --> 01:37:26,380
will be able to move behind the rebel lines where it's safe.

1320
01:37:26,460 --> 01:37:28,510
The Interhamwe, what about them?

1321
01:37:28,580 --> 01:37:31,920
-No one controls them. -This time they will kill us all.

1322
01:37:31,990 --> 01:37:34,390
They will kill us all if we stay here.

1323
01:37:35,060 --> 01:37:36,790
We have to take the chance.

1324
01:37:37,730 --> 01:37:39,720
What time should we be ready to leave?

1325
01:37:40,670 --> 01:37:42,760
I can put it together in two days, Paul.

1326
01:37:42,840 --> 01:37:44,100
Two days?

1327
01:37:44,930 --> 01:37:47,660
Colonel, there is no way that we can hold out for two days.

1328
01:37:47,740 --> 01:37:49,530
I have nothing left to bribe them with.

1329
01:37:51,070 --> 01:37:55,140
Colonel, we will all be dead in two days.

1330
01:38:18,770 --> 01:38:21,930
Diane... let your mother rest.

1331
01:38:22,010 --> 01:38:24,340
You rest too, sweetheart. Go to sleep.

1332
01:38:33,190 --> 01:38:34,410
Diplomat.

1333
01:38:36,420 --> 01:38:37,470
What?

1334
01:38:38,390 --> 01:38:40,320
I have to go to the Diplomat.

1335
01:38:50,630 --> 01:38:53,500
-What are you doing? -We have to go to the Diplomat.

1336
01:38:53,570 --> 01:38:56,100
-To do what? -Your items, they are there.

1337
01:38:57,550 --> 01:39:00,030
Will you please put your policemen at the gate, sir?

1338
01:39:00,110 --> 01:39:03,010
No. Let us see what you have to offer first.

1339
01:39:14,460 --> 01:39:16,620
Oh, no. Madame Archer.

1340
01:39:34,480 --> 01:39:35,470
Move, move!

1341
01:39:40,920 --> 01:39:42,250
-Cover us. -Yes, sir.

1342
01:39:42,320 --> 01:39:43,310
Hurry!

1343
01:39:47,660 --> 01:39:48,950
Come on, show me.

1344
01:39:58,170 --> 01:40:01,010
Look at this. Nice, yes?

1345
01:40:01,780 --> 01:40:03,100
And here you are.

1346
01:40:09,910 --> 01:40:12,480
The rebels are getting closer, yes?

1347
01:40:13,350 --> 01:40:15,880
The rebels can have this graveyard.

1348
01:40:15,960 --> 01:40:18,280
We have ordered everyone out of the city.

1349
01:40:21,030 --> 01:40:22,180
Here.

1350
01:40:23,300 --> 01:40:24,520
Have a drink.

1351
01:40:31,310 --> 01:40:33,300
You know what the Scottish call it?

1352
01:40:33,370 --> 01:40:34,860
No.

1353
01:40:36,710 --> 01:40:40,110
"Uisge beatha"... water of life.

1354
01:40:46,320 --> 01:40:52,260
I went once on a tour of the finest single malt distillery in the world.

1355
01:40:53,120 --> 01:40:56,060
-Have you ever been to Scotland? -No, sir.

1356
01:40:57,200 --> 01:40:58,690
Wonderful country.

1357
01:40:59,430 --> 01:41:01,020
Wonderful golf.

1358
01:41:02,270 --> 01:41:05,360
I wonder, will I ever go back?

1359
01:41:07,010 --> 01:41:08,270
What do you think?

1360
01:41:09,640 --> 01:41:10,810
No.

1361
01:41:12,410 --> 01:41:15,400
I hope we all get to do a great many things, General.

1362
01:41:16,920 --> 01:41:18,470
Can we go now, please, sir?

1363
01:41:20,220 --> 01:41:22,880
I am going to do you a great favor, Paul.

1364
01:41:22,980 --> 01:41:24,920
-Private. -Yes, sir!

1365
01:41:24,990 --> 01:41:28,190
Pack those carefully, put them in my jeep, and guard them.

1366
01:41:28,960 --> 01:41:33,480
I am going to take you with us to our new headquarters in Gitarama.

1367
01:41:34,270 --> 01:41:36,360
I do not want to go to Gitarama, sir.

1368
01:41:36,440 --> 01:41:39,090
Well, you can't go back to the hotel.

1369
01:41:39,170 --> 01:41:41,000
The crazy men are on their way there now.

1370
01:41:41,080 --> 01:41:46,480
Sir... General, we must go back so that I can get my family.

1371
01:41:46,550 --> 01:41:49,680
Trust me, we are better off here.

1372
01:41:49,750 --> 01:41:54,620
General, these are difficult times.

1373
01:41:54,680 --> 01:41:56,490
We need to help one another.

1374
01:41:56,560 --> 01:41:59,890
And what help can I get from you, Paul?

1375
01:41:59,960 --> 01:42:03,390
-You are a marked man, sir. -How so?

1376
01:42:03,460 --> 01:42:07,260
You are on a list. The Americans have you on their list as a war criminal.

1377
01:42:07,330 --> 01:42:10,320
Paul, I am sick and tired of your lies.

1378
01:42:10,410 --> 01:42:13,170
Are you stupid, General?

1379
01:42:13,240 --> 01:42:15,430
How do you think these people operate?

1380
01:42:15,510 --> 01:42:19,970
You sit here with five stars on your chest. Who do you think they are coming after?

1381
01:42:24,590 --> 01:42:25,740
Fine.

1382
01:42:27,150 --> 01:42:31,080
We will go to Gitarama, and you will stay on that list.

1383
01:42:31,160 --> 01:42:35,060
-I committed no war crimes. -Who will tell them?

1384
01:42:35,130 --> 01:42:38,060
You need me to tell them how you helped at the hotel.

1385
01:42:38,130 --> 01:42:41,360
They blame you for all their misfortunes. They say you led the massacres.

1386
01:42:41,440 --> 01:42:42,920
I led no massacres!

1387
01:42:43,000 --> 01:42:44,930
Do you think they're going to believe you?

1388
01:42:45,000 --> 01:42:46,530
You will tell them the truth!

1389
01:42:46,610 --> 01:42:48,800
I will tell them nothing unless you help me.

1390
01:42:50,640 --> 01:42:53,070
What are you going to do, shoot me?

1391
01:42:55,120 --> 01:42:56,440
Shoot me.

1392
01:42:57,080 --> 01:42:59,210
Please shoot me. It would be a blessing.

1393
01:42:59,290 --> 01:43:02,620
I will pay you to shoot my family.

1394
01:43:03,630 --> 01:43:04,950
You cannot hurt me.

1395
01:43:05,020 --> 01:43:08,580
You will tell them that I did nothing!

1396
01:43:11,330 --> 01:43:14,200
We are leaving. Right now.

1397
01:43:23,040 --> 01:43:25,010
Get out!

1398
01:43:27,320 --> 01:43:29,370
Get these people away from the gate!

1399
01:43:35,220 --> 01:43:37,270
Stop it! Stop it!

1400
01:43:37,950 --> 01:43:39,290
Clear the hotel.

1401
01:43:40,060 --> 01:43:42,220
-Tatiana! -Get out of here!

1402
01:43:42,290 --> 01:43:43,690
-Get out! -Tatiana!

1403
01:43:44,500 --> 01:43:45,760
Get out!

1404
01:43:47,130 --> 01:43:50,760
All of the militia must leave now! Get out!

1405
01:44:12,360 --> 01:44:13,520
Oh, no, no!

1406
01:44:13,590 --> 01:44:15,080
Shut up, cockroach! Get down!

1407
01:44:17,600 --> 01:44:19,460
That's him. That's him!

1408
01:44:20,600 --> 01:44:22,730
-Shit. -That's the manager!

1409
01:44:22,800 --> 01:44:26,060
-Stop him. Stop him! -I got him! I got him!

1410
01:44:37,350 --> 01:44:39,370
Stay where you are!

1411
01:44:56,360 --> 01:44:57,990
Tatiana!

1412
01:44:59,300 --> 01:45:01,040
Tatiana!

1413
01:45:07,010 --> 01:45:09,270
-Have you seen Tatiana? -No, I've not seen Tatiana.

1414
01:45:09,350 --> 01:45:11,840
-Paul, what is happening? -I have to find my wife!

1415
01:45:14,150 --> 01:45:15,280
Tatiana!

1416
01:45:19,290 --> 01:45:20,450
Tatiana!

1417
01:45:47,220 --> 01:45:48,980
They've gone. They've gone.

1418
01:45:51,330 --> 01:45:52,320
They've gone.

1419
01:45:57,230 --> 01:45:59,220
What were you going to do with this?

1420
01:46:08,940 --> 01:46:10,880
I thought you had...

1421
01:46:10,940 --> 01:46:12,740
I thought you had jumped.

1422
01:46:24,920 --> 01:46:27,080
Everyone on the trucks, please.

1423
01:46:27,150 --> 01:46:29,930
Take your luggage. Families please stay together.

1424
01:46:29,990 --> 01:46:32,860
-Oh, please. -As fast as you can, everyone. Please.

1425
01:46:32,930 --> 01:46:35,370
There's enough room for everyone.

1426
01:46:38,670 --> 01:46:40,530
I hope someday we will come back.

1427
01:46:41,770 --> 01:46:42,970
Let's move out.

1428
01:46:53,010 --> 01:46:55,110
What is wrong with her?

1429
01:46:55,790 --> 01:46:57,880
She has a very high fever.

1430
01:47:05,700 --> 01:47:08,160
Where are we going, Daddy?

1431
01:47:08,240 --> 01:47:09,860
Someplace safe.

1432
01:48:07,660 --> 01:48:08,890
My God.

1433
01:48:31,280 --> 01:48:32,870
What's happening?

1434
01:48:57,680 --> 01:49:00,870
Come on, let's go. Children on the ground. Bring the children this way.

1435
01:49:00,940 --> 01:49:03,200
Pass them back, pass them back.

1436
01:49:09,280 --> 01:49:12,450
Do not stop. Do not stop! Go right on through.

1437
01:49:24,840 --> 01:49:26,270
Get down!

1438
01:49:28,970 --> 01:49:30,100
Stay down!

1439
01:49:53,630 --> 01:49:55,120
What's happening there?

1440
01:49:58,640 --> 01:50:02,130
It's the rebels. We're crossing the front line.

1441
01:50:03,110 --> 01:50:05,870
It's okay. We're safe.

1442
01:50:05,940 --> 01:50:07,070
It's okay.

1443
01:50:07,140 --> 01:50:09,140
It's okay, you are safe here. You are safe.

1444
01:50:09,210 --> 01:50:12,840
It's okay now. Sit back down.

1445
01:50:14,620 --> 01:50:15,780
Hello.

1446
01:50:46,490 --> 01:50:48,310
Get some more water.

1447
01:50:49,580 --> 01:50:52,570
The doctor says he is very dehydrated.

1448
01:50:52,660 --> 01:50:55,180
We made it. Come on, let's get down.

1449
01:50:56,530 --> 01:50:58,360
-Come on. -It is okay.

1450
01:50:58,420 --> 01:51:00,160
-She is sick. -Okay.

1451
01:51:01,140 --> 01:51:02,600
Yeah, she's very sick. Take her.

1452
01:51:05,040 --> 01:51:09,370
Paul, the buses are on the other side of camp.

1453
01:51:09,440 --> 01:51:11,800
They'll take you to Tanzania.

1454
01:51:11,880 --> 01:51:15,680
Go now, Paul, 'cause I don't know when there'd be another opportunity.

1455
01:51:15,740 --> 01:51:17,080
-Thank you. -Yeah.

1456
01:51:17,150 --> 01:51:19,380
-Good luck. -Thank you.

1457
01:51:22,350 --> 01:51:24,350
-Thank God. -We made it.

1458
01:51:24,420 --> 01:51:26,980
Please, please. We are here, yeah?

1459
01:51:27,060 --> 01:51:28,680
-Thank you, Paul. -We have made it.

1460
01:51:28,760 --> 01:51:30,750
-Thank you. -Yes, yes. Come.

1461
01:51:31,230 --> 01:51:32,220
Mr. Manager.

1462
01:51:32,290 --> 01:51:34,700
-I just want to thank you. -Of course, Steven.

1463
01:51:34,760 --> 01:51:35,860
Constance!

1464
01:51:36,800 --> 01:51:39,570
Thank God you are alive! It's so good to see you.

1465
01:51:39,630 --> 01:51:42,120
Have you seen my brother and his wife?

1466
01:51:42,210 --> 01:51:43,370
None of them.

1467
01:51:44,150 --> 01:51:46,630
Has anyone seen these people? You don't recog...

1468
01:51:46,710 --> 01:51:49,050
Mama, come see quick.

1469
01:51:49,110 --> 01:51:51,580
-Excuse me, excuse me. -Can you see them anywhere?

1470
01:51:53,580 --> 01:51:55,180
Here, Mama, look.

1471
01:51:55,250 --> 01:51:56,510
Please.

1472
01:51:58,160 --> 01:52:01,420
Do you see them, Mama? Is that them?

1473
01:52:02,120 --> 01:52:03,930
Is that them, Mama?

1474
01:52:05,260 --> 01:52:07,360
Do you recognize these people?

1475
01:52:07,430 --> 01:52:10,560
This little girl, she's Anais, and this is Carine.

1476
01:52:10,630 --> 01:52:12,120
Do you recognize them?

1477
01:52:13,870 --> 01:52:17,570
-Ma'am, have you seen these girls? -No, no, I haven't.

1478
01:52:17,640 --> 01:52:19,810
Have any of you seen these girls?

1479
01:52:22,250 --> 01:52:24,940
Anais. And that's my brother.

1480
01:52:25,010 --> 01:52:27,000
Everybody on the buses!

1481
01:52:35,760 --> 01:52:37,780
Can you feel anything when I touch here?

1482
01:52:37,860 --> 01:52:39,890
Everybody on the buses!

1483
01:52:39,960 --> 01:52:42,560
Can you move out of the way? We need some room here!

1484
01:52:42,630 --> 01:52:45,970
-We'll find the girls, Tatsi. We will. -Okay.

1485
01:52:49,910 --> 01:52:51,540
Boussey?

1486
01:52:51,610 --> 01:52:52,950
It's you.

1487
01:52:56,010 --> 01:52:57,500
Where'd you find this child?

1488
01:52:57,590 --> 01:52:59,910
They just arrived on trucks from the Mille Collines.

1489
01:53:02,120 --> 01:53:06,050
All Mille Collines evacuees to the buses now, please.

1490
01:53:06,120 --> 01:53:08,120
-Oh, no. -We need to hurry up, please.

1491
01:53:14,500 --> 01:53:16,830
Come on, get some sleep.

1492
01:53:18,030 --> 01:53:19,160
Wait!

1493
01:53:28,810 --> 01:53:30,640
Hold it, please!

1494
01:53:33,410 --> 01:53:35,110
-Tatiana! -It's Pat!

1495
01:53:35,190 --> 01:53:37,660
-Tatiana! -Madame Archer!

1496
01:53:37,720 --> 01:53:40,450
Stop the bus! Stop the bus, stop the bus!

1497
01:53:40,520 --> 01:53:41,680
Come. Come, come.

1498
01:53:42,560 --> 01:53:44,260
Please, wait for us.

1499
01:53:44,330 --> 01:53:47,170
Madame Archer. I was so worried. I thought...

1500
01:53:48,400 --> 01:53:50,340
It's wonderful to see you.

1501
01:53:50,400 --> 01:53:51,840
Come quickly.

1502
01:53:59,270 --> 01:54:01,640
-Carine? -Anais?

1503
01:54:01,710 --> 01:54:02,940
Anais?

1504
01:54:03,020 --> 01:54:05,710
Just wait. It's gonna be just a minute now.

1505
01:54:07,610 --> 01:54:10,050
Anais? Carine?

1506
01:54:24,730 --> 01:54:26,730
Oh, my God!

1507
01:54:28,040 --> 01:54:30,060
Oh, my God!

1508
01:54:30,140 --> 01:54:32,080
Come, come, come!

1509
01:54:35,610 --> 01:54:39,550
Hello, Carine. Anais, hello. How are you, sweetheart?

1510
01:54:41,890 --> 01:54:43,550
Do you see your cousins?

1511
01:54:51,400 --> 01:54:53,760
They said there wasn't any room.

1512
01:54:53,830 --> 01:54:55,490
There's always room.

1513
01:55:10,770 --> 01:55:17,070
保罗·卢斯赛伯吉纳保护了基加利米勒·科林斯饭店的
１２６８名图西族和胡图族难民

1514
01:55:18,770 --> 01:55:25,960
保罗和塔莎娜还有他们的孩子罗杰 黛安 伊利 特丽莎
以及他们收养的侄女
爱耐丝和卡琳现在住在比利时

1515
01:55:27,770 --> 01:55:32,270
塔莎娜的哥哥托马斯和他的妻子费登丝
尚未被发现

1516
01:55:34,170 --> 01:55:40,570
２００２年奥古斯丁·比齐蒙戈将军
在安哥拉被逮捕并运往联合国坦桑尼亚
的战争犯罪法庭同一法庭上
部落民兵领袖乔治·卢塔甘达
被判处终身监禁

1517
01:55:42,470 --> 01:55:49,270
种族屠杀于１９９４年７月结束
此时图西族叛乱分子将胡图族军队
及部族民兵驱赶到了刚果边境

